  id:"blackfootmt", name:"Blackfoot River", color:"#3a8c5b",
  state:"MT", region:"montana", gauges:["blackfootNevadaCr","blackfootBonner"], primaryGauge:"blackfootNevadaCr",
  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  osmName:"Blackfoot River",
  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"<b>Mainstem and all tributaries except the Clearwater River. During the General Season (third Saturday in May through Nov. 30)</b><br>• Catch-and-release for cutthroat trout.<br>• Combined trout: 3 daily and in possession, Only 1 rainbow trout over 14 inches long, any size brown trout. (See Clearwater River Drainage for exception.)<br>• Artificial lures only within 100-yard radius of the mouths of Belmont Creek, Copper Creek, Gold Creek, Monture Creek and North Fork Blackfoot River.<br><b>Mainstem only during the Extended Season (Dec. 1 to the third Saturday in May)</b><br>• Extended season for mountain whitefish and catch-and-release for trout open Dec. 1 to third Saturday in May. Tributaries are closed to fishing during the extended season.<br>• Artificial lures and/or maggots only.<br>• All other live/dead bait prohibited.<br><b>Mainstem from Landers Fork mouth downstream to the confluence with the Clark Fork River</b><br>• Catch-and-release for brook trout. (This regulation is a result of bull trout being misidentified and harvested as brook trout. Brook trout are very rare in this section of river whereas bull trout are common.)<br><br><b>Western District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open the third Saturday in May through Nov. 30. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 14 inches. Cutthroat trout: 3 daily and in possession, none over 12 inches. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession. All waters are closed to angling for bull trout, and all must be released without delay.",
