  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"<b>Upstream from Perkins Lane Bridge, near Warm Springs</b><br>• Open entire year.<br>• Catch-and-release only.<br>• Artificial lures only.<br>• Closed to fishing from boats/vessels.<br><b>Perkins Lane Bridge, near Warm Springs, to mouth of the Flathead River During the General Season (third Saturday in May through Nov. 30)</b><br>• Catch-and-release for cutthroat trout.<br>• Northern pike: no limit.<br>• Combined trout: 3 daily and in possession, Only 1 over 14 inches long.<br>• Artificial lures only within a 100-yard radius of the mouths of Rattlesnake Creek, Petty Creek, Fish Creek, Cedar Creek, Dry Creek, Trout Creek and St. Regis River.<br><b>During the Extended Season (Dec. 1 to the third Saturday in May)</b><br>• Extended season for northern pike and whitefish and catch-and-release for trout open Dec. 1 to third Saturday in May.<br>• Artificial lures and/or maggots only.<br>• All other live/dead bait prohibited. temporary/seasonal angling restrictions and closures not listed here.<br><br><b>Western District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open the third Saturday in May through Nov. 30. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 14 inches. Cutthroat trout: 3 daily and in possession, none over 12 inches. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession. All waters are closed to angling for bull trout, and all must be released without delay.",
