  id:"nfblackfoot", name:"North Fork Blackfoot River", color:"#8a6a2f",
  state:"MT", region:"montana", gauges:["nfblackfootDryGulch"], primaryGauge:"nfblackfootDryGulch",
  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  osmName:"North Fork Blackfoot River",
  parkRegsSrc:"montana",
  parkRegs:"<b>Downstream from the North Fork Falls</b><br>• Artificial lures only, including within a 100-yard radius of the mouth.<br><b>From North Fork Falls downstream to Highway 200 bridge</b><br>• Artificial lures with single point barbless hooks only.<br><b>Entire river</b><br>• Catch-and-release for cutthroat trout.<br>• Combined trout: 3 daily and in possession, Only 1 rainbow trout over 14 inches, any size brown trout.<br><br><b>Western District standard rules</b> — rivers and streams open the third Saturday in May through Nov. 30. Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden trout and arctic grayling): 3 daily and in possession, only 1 over 14 inches. Cutthroat trout: 3 daily and in possession, none over 12 inches. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession. All waters are closed to angling for bull trout, and all must be released without delay.",
