  osmName:"Sacramento River",
  parkRegsSrc:"california",
  parkRegs:"<b>Sacramento River and tributaries above Keswick Dam</b><br>• (Shasta and Siskiyou cos.).<br><b>Sacramento River and tributaries from Box Canyon Dam downstream to the Scarlett Way bridge in Dunsmuir.</b><br>• All year. Only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used. <i>Bag: 0 trout</i><br><b>Sacramento River and tributaries from Scarlett Way bridge downstream to the county bridge at Sweetbriar.</b><br>• Sat. preceding Memorial Day through Sep. 30. <i>Bag: 5 trout</i><br>• Oct. 1 through the Fri. preceding Memorial Day. Only artificial lures may be used. <i>Bag: 2 trout</i><br><b>Sacramento River and tributaries from the county bridge at Sweetbriar downstream to Shasta Lake.</b><br>• All year. Only artificial lures may be used. <i>Bag: 2 trout</i><br><br><b>California statewide stream rule</b> (§5.85) — open the last Saturday in April through November 15 with a five-trout daily bag and ten-trout possession limit, no gear restrictions. From November 16 through the Friday preceding the last Saturday in April, a zero-trout bag limit applies and only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used; trout must be released unharmed and should not be removed from the water.",
