  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  osmName:"South Fork Eel River",
  parkRegsSrc:"california",
  parkRegs:"<i>Salmon and steelhead water.</i> This river is listed in CDFW's 2026 anadromous-water regulations, <b>§7.40(b)(40)</b>, with reach-by-reach seasons, barbless-hook rules and hatchery-only harvest limits that change through the year. Those tables are reproduced here only by reference — read that entry in the current booklet before you fish.<br>• <b>Low-flow closures (§8.00(a)):</b> from September 1 through April 30 the Eel, Mad, Mattole, Redwood Creek, Smith and Van Duzen close to all angling on set days whenever CDFW finds flows below minimums at designated gauges — check CDFW's low-flow hotline before driving out.<br><br><b>California statewide stream rule</b> (§5.85) — open the last Saturday in April through November 15 with a five-trout daily bag and ten-trout possession limit, no gear restrictions. From November 16 through the Friday preceding the last Saturday in April, a zero-trout bag limit applies and only artificial lures with barbless hooks may be used; trout must be released unharmed and should not be removed from the water.",
