  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  osmName:"Deschutes River",
  parkRegsSrc:"oregon",
  parkRegs:"<b>I-84 bridge to Sherars Falls</b><br>• Open all year for trout and hatchery steelhead.<br>• 2 rainbow trout per day, 10 inch minimum and 13 inch maximum length.<br>• Open for Chinook salmon Aug 1 - Oct 31.<br>• Open for coho salmon Aug 1 - Dec 31.<br>• Bait allowed only from Sherars Falls downstream to upper trestle (approx. 3 Mi).<br>• No angling from a floating device.<br>• Closed from Sherars Falls downstream to Buck Hollow Cr (approx. 1 Mi) Apr 1 - Jul 31.<br><b>Sherars Falls to Northern Boundary of the Warm Springs Reservation (including White River upstream to first falls)</b><br>• Open all year for trout and hatchery steelhead.<br>• 2 rainbow trout per day, 10 inch minimum and 13 inch maximum length.<br>• Open for coho salmon Aug 1 - Dec 31.<br>• No angling from a floating device.<br><b>Northern Boundary of the Warm Springs Reservation to the Pelton Regulating Reservoir.</b><br>• Open Apr 22 - Dec 31 for trout and hatchery steelhead.<br>• 2 rainbow trout per day, 10 inch minimum and 13 inch maximum length.<br>• Open for coho salmon Aug 1 - Dec 31.<br>• No angling from a floating device.<br>• See Lake Simtustus.<br>• Closed from Pelton Regulating Dam downstream approx. 600 ft to ODFW markers.<br><br><b>Central Zone standard rules</b> — streams open May 22 – Oct 31 unless noted under Exceptions. 2 trout per day, 3 daily limits in possession, 8 inch minimum length, only 1 trout over 20 inches per day. Angling restricted to artificial flies and lures in streams unless an exception allows bait. Rainbow trout over 20 inches are considered steelhead in streams.",
