  parkRegs:"<b>Mouth to Chiloquin Bridge</b><br>• Open May 22 - Oct 31.<br>• Catch-and-release for rainbow trout.<br>• Only single point hooks may be used.<br><b>Chiloquin Bridge to Kirk Rd Bridge</b><br>• Open May 22 - Oct 31.<br>• Catch-and-release for rainbow trout.<br>• Only single point hooks may be used.<br>• No angling from a floating device.<br><b>Kirk Rd Bridge to headwaters</b><br>• Catch-and-release for rainbow trout.<br>• Only single point hooks may be used.<br>• No angling from a floating device.<br><br><b>Southeast Zone standard rules</b> — streams open all year unless noted under Exceptions. 2 trout per day, 3 daily limits in possession, 8 inch minimum length, only 1 trout over 20 inches per day. Angling restricted to artificial flies and lures in streams unless an exception allows bait. No limit on size or number of brook or brown trout in streams unless noted. Closed to angling for bull trout.",
