  id:"methow", name:"Methow River", color:"#4f8f6f",
  state:"WA", region:"washington", gauges:["methowGoatCreek","methowWinthrop","methowTwisp","methowPateros"], primaryGauge:"methowTwisp",
  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  osmName:"Methow River",
  parkRegsSrc:"washington",
  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 30 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>from mouth to County Rd. 1535 (Burma Rd.) Bridge</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: CLOSED WATERS. tributaries from mouth to County Rd. 1535 (Burma Rd.) Bridge except Black Canyon Creek<br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). Eastern brook<br>• <b>trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 No min. size. No daily limit.<br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: (hatchery) Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Closed.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Catch-and-release.<br><b>from County Rd. 1535 (Burma Rd.) Bridge to Gold Creek CRC (621)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Selective gear rules.<br>• <b>All game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Sept. 15 Catch-and-release.<br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: (hatchery) Sat. before Memorial Day-Sept. 15 Closed. tributaries from the County Rd. 1535 (Burma Rd.) Bridge to Gold Creek, except Gold Creek<br>• <b>All species</b>: Selective gear rules. Eastern brook<br>• <b>trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 No min. size. No daily limit.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Catch-and-release.<br><b>from Gold Creek to Foghorn Dam CRC (621)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Internal combustion motors prohibited. Selective gear rules.<br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: (hatchery) Sat. before Memorial Day-Sept. 30 Closed.<br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: Dec. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Whitefish gear rules. Open for whitefish only.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Sept. 30 Catch-and-release. all tributaries from Gold Creek to Foghorn Dam except Beaver Creek, Chewuch River, Libby Creek, and Twisp River Eastern brook<br>• <b>trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 No min. size. No daily limit.<br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: (hatchery) Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Closed.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Catch-and-release.<br><b>from Foghorn Dam to Weeman Bridge, including tributaries except Wolf Creek</b><br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: (hatchery) Sat. before Memorial Day-Aug. 15 Closed. (Continued on next column) (Continued on next page) SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES<br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: Dec. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Whitefish gear rules. Open for whitefish only.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Aug. 15 Catch-and-release. Selective gear rules.<br><b>from Weeman Bridge to the falls above Brush Creek CRC (621)</b><br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: Dec. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Whitefish gear rules. Open for whitefish only. all tributaries from Weeman Bridge to the falls above Brush Creek except Lost River, Goat Creek, and Early Winters Creek<br>• <b>All species</b>: Selective gear rules.<br>• <b>Steelhead</b>: (hatchery) Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Closed.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Catch-and-release.</details><br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
