  osmName:"Entiat River",
  parkRegsSrc:"washington",
  parkRegs:"<b>from mouth (railroad bridge) to the boundary marker/markers located approx. 1500’</b><br><b>upstream of the upper Roaring Creek Rd. Bridge (immediately downstream of the Entiat National Fish Hatchery) CRC (586)</b><br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: Dec. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Whitefish gear rules. Open for whitefish only.<br><b>from the boundary marker/markers located approx. 1500’ upstream of the upper Roaring Creek Rd. Bridge (immediately downstream of the Entiat National Fish Hatchery) to Entiat Falls</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older).<br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: Dec. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Whitefish gear rules. Open for whitefish only.<br><b>from Entiat Falls upstream and all tributaries</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Selective gear rules.<br>• <b>All game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES<br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
