  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 33 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>from mouth to 2,500' downstream of the boat ramp below Lewis St. Bridge at Monroe CRC (844)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Anti-snagging rule. Night closure. Selective gear rules, except only one single-point barbless hook allowed. Dolly varden/<br>• <b>bull trout</b>: Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Min. size 20\". May be retained as part of trout daily limit. Other trout Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Daily limit 2. Release Chinook and chum.<br><b>from 2,500' downstream boat ramp below Lewis St. Bridge at Monroe to the boat ramp CRC (844)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Night closure. Selective gear rules, except only one single-point barbless hook allowed. Anti-snagging rule. Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Fishing from any floating device prohibited. SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES Dolly varden/<br>• <b>bull trout</b>: Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Min. size 20\". May be retained as part of trout daily limit. Other trout Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Daily limit 2. Release Chinook and chum.<br><b>from the boat ramp below the Lewis St. Bridge in Monroe to Wallace River CRC (844)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Night closure. Selective gear rules, except only one single-point barbless hook allowed. Anti-snagging rule. Dolly varden/<br>• <b>bull trout</b>: Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Min. size 20\". May be retained as part of trout daily limit. Other trout Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Daily limit 2. Release Chinook and chum.<br><b>from Wallace River upstream to Railroad Bridge at Big Eddy CRC (844)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Selective gear rules, except only one single-point barb- less hook allowed. Night closure. Anti-snagging rule. Dolly varden/<br>• <b>bull trout</b>: Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Min. size 20\". May be retained as part of trout daily limit. Other trout Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Nov. 1-Jan. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Salmon</b>: Nov. 1-Nov. 30 Daily limit 2. Release Chinook and chum.<br><b>from Railroad Bridge at Big Eddy to 1,000' Downstream of Reiter Ponds outlet CRC (844) Dolly varden/</b><br>• <b>bull trout</b>: Nov. 1-Feb. 15 Min. size 20\". May be retained as part of trout daily limit.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Nov. 1-Feb. 15 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Nov. 1-Feb. 15 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br><b>from 1,000' downstream of Reiter Ponds outlet to 1,500' upstream of Reiter Ponds outlet CRC (844)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Fishing from any floating device prohibited. Dolly varden/<br>• <b>bull trout</b>: Nov. 1-Feb. 15 Min. size 20\". May be retained as part of trout daily limit.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Nov. 1-Feb. 15 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Nov. 1-Feb. 15 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br><b>from 1,500' upstream of the Reiter Ponds outlet to confluence of North and South forks CRC (844) Dolly varden/</b><br>• <b>bull trout</b>: Nov. 1-Feb. 15 Min. size 20\". May be retained as part of trout daily limit.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Nov. 1-Feb. 15 Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: Cutthroat trout and wild rainbow trout: min. size 14\".<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Nov. 1-Feb. 15 Statewide min. size/daily limit.</details><br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
