  id:"windwa", name:"Wind River (WA)", color:"#5f6f9f",
  state:"WA", region:"washington", gauges:["windCarson"], primaryGauge:"windCarson",
  geom:"osm",   // OpenStreetMap channel, clipped to the state with park water removed — don't re-snap
  osmName:"Wind River",
  parkRegsSrc:"washington",
  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 27 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>from boundary line markers at mouth to Hwy. 14 Bridge CRC (680)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). Mar. 16-June 30 Night closure. Each angler aboard a vessel may deploy salmon/steelhead angling gear until the daily salmon/steelhead limit for all anglers aboard has been achieved. Anglers may fish with 2 poles for salmon and steelhead with 2-Pole Endorsement. July 1-Oct. 31 Night closure for salmon and steelhead fishing only. Aug. 1-Oct. 31 Anti-snagging rule.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Year-round Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: release cut- throat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Year-round Statewide min. size/daily limit. Salmon and hatchery<br>• <b>steelhead</b>: Mar. 16-June 30 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adult salmon or 2 hatchery steelhead or 1 of each. Release wild Chinook and wild coho. July 1-Sept. 30 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 salmon including no more than 2 adults. Release wild Chinook and wild coho. Closed to fishing for or retaining steelhead. Oct. 1-Oct. 31 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 salmon including no more than 2 adults. Release wild coho. Closed to fishing for or retaining steelhead. Nov. 1-Mar. 15 Daily limit 3 hatchery steelhead. Release all salmon.<br><b>from Hwy. 14 Bridge to 400’ downstream of Shipherd Falls fish ladder CRC (679)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). Mar. 16-June 30 Night closure. May 1-June 30 Anti-snagging rule. July 1-Oct. 31 Night closure for salmon and steelhead fishing only. Aug. 1-Oct. 31 Anti-snagging rule.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Year-round Statewide min. size/daily limit. Except: release cut- throat trout and wild rainbow trout.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Year-round Statewide min. size/daily limit. Salmon and hatchery<br>• <b>steelhead</b>: Mar. 16-June 30 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adult salmon or 2 hatchery steelhead or 1 of each. Release wild Chinook and wild coho. July 1-Oct. 31 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 salmon including no more than 2 adults. Release wild Chinook and wild coho. Closed to fishing for or retaining steelhead. Nov. 1-Mar. 15 Min. size 20”. Daily limit 3 hatchery steelhead. Release all salmon.<br><b>from 400’ below to 100’ above Shipherd Falls fish ladder</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: CLOSED WATERS.<br><b>from 100’ above Shipherd Falls to 400’ below Coffer Dam (at river mile 2.93, -121.812619, 45.745576) CRC (677)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Anti-snagging rule. Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). Night closure. Sept. 16-Nov. 30 Selective gear rules, except barbed hooks are allowed.<br>• <b>All game fish</b>: Sept. 16-Nov. 30 Catch-and-release. Salmon and hatchery<br>• <b>steelhead</b>: May 1-June 30 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adult salmon or 2 hatchery steelhead or 1 of each.<br><b>from 400’ below to 100’ above Coffer Dam (at river mile 2.93, -121.812619, 45.745576)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: CLOSED WATERS.<br><b>from 100’ above Coffer Dam to 800 yards downstream of Carson National Fish Hatchery CRC (677)</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). Night closure. Anti-snagging rule. Sept. 16-Nov. 30 Selective gear rules, except barbed hooks are allowed. SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES<br>• <b>All game fish</b>: Sept. 16-Nov. 30 Catch-and-release. Salmon and hatchery<br>• <b>steelhead</b>: May 1-June 30 Min. size 12”. Daily limit 6 including no more than 2 adult salmon or 2 hatchery steelhead or 1 of each.<br><b>from 800 yards downstream of Carson National Fish Hatchery to Moore Bridge</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Columbia River Salmon and Steelhead Endorsement (CRSSE) required for salmon and steelhead fishing (ages 15 and older). Selective gear rules, except barbed hooks are allowed.<br>• <b>All game fish</b>: Sept. 16-Nov. 30 Catch-and-release.<br><b>from Moore Bridge upstream</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: CLOSED WATERS.</details><br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
