  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 16 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>from Barstow Bridge upstream to U.S.- Canadian border</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Internal combustion motors prohibited. Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Selective gear rules.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Min. size 14”. Daily limit 2.<br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: Nov. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Whitefish gear rules. Open for whitefish only. (Continued on next column) (Continued on next page) SPECIES DATE ADDITIONAL RULES<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br>• <b>Sturgeon</b>: Year-round Closed.<br><b>from Canadian border upstream to Hwy. 21 Bridge at Curlew</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Internal combustion motors prohibited. Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Selective gear rules, except for juvenile anglers (under the age of 15).<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Min. size 14”. Daily limit 2.<br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: Nov. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Whitefish gear rules. Open for whitefish only.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.<br><b>from Hwy. 21 Bridge at Curlew upstream to Canadian border</b><br>• <b>All species</b>: Internal combustion motors prohibited. Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Selective gear rules.<br>• <b>Trout</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Min. size 14”. Daily limit 2.<br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: Nov. 1-Last Day of Feb. Statewide min. size/daily limit. Whitefish gear rules. Open for whitefish only.<br>• <b>Other game fish</b>: Sat. before Memorial Day-Oct. 31 Statewide min. size/daily limit.</details><br><br><b>Washington statewide freshwater rules</b> — rivers, streams and beaver ponds open the Saturday before Memorial Day through October 31. Brown, cutthroat, rainbow, golden and tiger trout and grayling: 8 inch minimum, daily limit 2. Eastern brook trout: no minimum, no daily limit. Dolly Varden/bull trout: closed unless listed in Special Rules. Release all wild steelhead.<br><br><i>Selective gear rules</i>: artificial flies or lures with barbless single-point hooks only, bait prohibited, up to 3 hooks, knotless nets only.",
