  parkRegsSrc:"michigan",
  parkRegs:"<b>Gear Restricted reaches</b> — On all streams managed under gear restrictions, it shall be unlawful to use or possess live bait, dead or preserved bait or organic or processed food on any of the waters or on shore. It shall be unlawful to use or possess scented material on flies-only Gear Restricted Streams.<br>• (Delta Co.) from Boney Falls Dam to Mouth of Silver Creek: Fishing Season: open all year; Possession Season: last Sat. in April – Sep. 30 for Brook Trout and Brown Trout; open all year for Rainbow Trout; Tackle: artificial lures only; Daily Possession Limit: 2 trout; Minimum Size Limits: Brook Trout — 10\"; Brown Trout and Rainbow Trout — 12\". Mileage: 14.2 miles.<br><br><b>Type 1 trout stream</b> — Fishing season: Last Sat. in April – Sep. 30. Possession season: Last Sat. in April – Sep. 30. Minimum size: Brook Trout 7\"; Brown Trout 8\"; Atlantic, Chinook, Coho &amp; Pink Salmon, Lake Trout, Rainbow Trout (Steelhead) &amp; Splake 10\". All trout and salmon daily possession limit: 5 fish, but no more than 3 trout 15\" or greater.<br><br><i>Reach boundaries and each reach's Type are on the DNR's Inland Trout &amp; Salmon maps (Michigan.gov/FishingMaps) and in the county listing, pp. 48–65 — which reach you're on decides which row applies.</i>",
