  osmName:"Montana Creek",
  parkRegsSrc:"alaska",
  parkRegs:"<b>MONTANA CREEK DRAINAGE:</b><br><b>Entire drainage including all waters within ½ mile radius of its confluence with the Susitna River:</b><br>• Rainbow/steelhead trout and Arctic grayling: Catch-and-release fishing only. All rainbow/ steelhead trout and Arctic grayling caught must be released immediately.<br>• From its mouth upstream to ADF&amp;G markers located ½ mile above the Parks Highway: King salmon: King salmon fishing is closed in 2026 by emergency order. June 1-July 13: Only unbaited, artificial lures or flies are allowed. Multiple hooks are allowed during this time, but only up to the Parks Highway. See EO restriction for May 1-July 13.<br>• July 14-August 31: Bait and multiple hooks are allowed, but only up to the Parks Highway.<br><b>Upstream of the Parks Highway:</b><br>• Only one unbaited, single-hook, artificial lure or fly is allowed year-round.<br><b>Upstream of ADF&amp;G markers located ½ mile above the Parks Highway:</b><br>• Closed year-round to all salmon fishing.<br>• Rainbow/steelhead trout and Arctic grayling: Catch-and-release fishing only. All rainbow/ steelhead trout and Arctic grayling caught must be released immediately. Sonia Praslowicz, burbot, Mat-Su Valley Matthew Kangas, chum salmon, Montana Creek<br><i>— ADF&amp;G 2026 Southcentral regulations, p. 21</i><br><br>Everything not covered above falls under the <b>Susitna River drainage (all units) general regulations</b> — ADF&amp;G 2026 Southcentral booklet, p. 15.",
