  parkRegsSrc:"alaska",
  parkRegs:"<b>NUYAKUK RIVER - from the outlet of Tikchik Lake to an island located about 2 miles downstream from Nuyakuk Falls:</b><br>• Open year-round to sport fishing for species other than king salmon.<br>• May 1-July 24: Open to king salmon fishing.<br>• Only unbaited, single-hook, artificial lures or flies may be used year-round.<br><i>— ADF&amp;G 2026 Southwest regulations, p. 14</i><br><br>Everything not covered above falls under the <b>Bristol Bay general regulations</b> — ADF&amp;G 2026 Southwest booklet, p. 10.",
