  parkRegsSrc:"grandcanyon",
  parkRegs:"A valid <b>Arizona fishing or combination licence</b> is required for resident and nonresident anglers ten years of age or older. No live baitfish may be used or in possession on any waters in Coconino County. Humpback chub, razorback sucker, bluehead sucker, flannelmouth sucker and speckled dace are protected statewide and may not be angled for, taken or possessed.<br><br><b>Colorado River</b><br>• From the Paria riffle to Navajo Bridge, including all tributaries. The limit is 6 rainbow trout per day. Rainbow trout taken from this portion of the Colorado River shall be killed and retained as part of the bag limit or immediately released.<br>• Closed to fishing: one-half mile upstream and one-half mile downstream from its confluence with the Little Colorado River.<br><br><b>Arizona statewide daily bag</b> — trout (includes rainbow, cutthroat, brown, brook, tiger, Gila and Apache trout; grayling): 4, any combination. The possession limit is two times the daily bag limit.<br><i>— AZGFD 2025 &amp; 2026 Fishing Regulations, Special Regulations and Seasons – Fish: Commission Order 40</i>",
