  parkRegsSrc:"arizona",
  parkRegs:"<b>Oak Creek</b><br>• Unlimited smallmouth and largemouth bass; unlimited channel and flathead catfish.<br>• Between the Highway 89A bridge crossing of Oak Creek at Slide Rock State Park upstream to the Sterling Springs Hatchery Property line including the West Fork Oak Creek and Oak Creek. Catch-and-release only for trout. Trout must be immediately released unharmed; no trout may be kept; artificial fly and lure only, barbless hooks only.<br><br><b>Arizona statewide daily bag</b> — trout (includes rainbow, cutthroat, brown, brook, tiger, Gila and Apache trout; grayling): 4, any combination. The possession limit is two times the daily bag limit.<br><i>— AZGFD 2025 &amp; 2026 Fishing Regulations, Special Regulations and Seasons – Fish: Commission Order 40</i>",
