  fish:"Blows out hard in runoff and clears late (July). Hopper water in August. Flows drop fast late season as irrigation pulls water — check the Kelly gauge before driving out. WGFD stream class: <b>Yellow Ribbon</b> — 50–299 lb of trout per mile. Game fish present, per WGFD: Brook Trout, Mountain Whitefish, RBT X CUT Hybrid, Rainbow Trout, Snake River Cutthroat. WGFD notes portions of this stream cross private land — public land is shaded on the map; check the Wading &amp; access row. The line follows WGFD's map of the whole river in Wyoming, about 109 km: about 6 km of it inside Grand Teton and the rest outside the park, under Wyoming's Area 1 rules. The gaps in it are Upper Slide Lake and Lower Slide Lake.",
