  blurb:"The Iowa DNR's Boone River Water Trail: 26.3 designated miles in Hamilton and Webster Counties, designated in June 2009. A wild, narrow river in a wooded corridor, where boulders the glaciers left make riffles that get tricky at low water and limestone, shale, coal and sandstone outcrops line the banks; seven mills once stood on it. It is a non-meandered stream: the state owns the water, not the bed or the banks, so away from the accesses and public land the shore is private. The DNR maps 7 access sites along it. The DNR has not yet rated the skill level of its 7 segments. The DNR's dam layer shows 1 dam on it (Briggs Woods Gaging Dam). (per Iowa DNR, 2026-10)",
