  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"The Iowa DNR's Des Moines River Water Trail: 89.3 designated miles in Webster and Boone Counties, designated in July 2009 (extended in September 2009). Bluffs, beaches and ravines through Fort Dodge, Dolliver Memorial State Park and Boone County; recent dam removals in Fort Dodge made the run through town safer, and at Fraser a built portage trail leads around the old hydroelectric dam from the North to the South Fraser access. It is a meandered stream: the bed, sandbars and banks below the high-water mark are public, and sandbar camping is allowed. The DNR maps 22 access sites along it, 2 of them fishing accesses rather than ramps. Of its 17 DNR segments, 1 Advanced and 16 not yet rated. The DNR's dam layer shows 3 dams on it (Trestle Weir, Lehigh Rock Dam and Boone Waterworks Dam), 1 with the portage side given. (per Iowa DNR, 2026-10)",
