  blurb:"The Iowa DNR's Maquoketa River Water Trail: 7.6 designated miles in Jones County, designated in October 2010. Bluffs and outcrops of ancient reef limestone in a corridor little changed since the glaciers; at low water a rocky riffle can mean walking the boat. It is a non-meandered stream: the state owns the water, not the bed or the banks, so away from the accesses and public land the shore is private. The DNR maps 2 access sites along it. The DNR rates its one segment Beginner. The DNR's dam layer shows no dam on it. (per Iowa DNR, 2026-10)",
