  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"The Iowa DNR's North Fork and Maquoketa River Water Trail: 16.0 designated miles in Jackson County, designated in June 2023. High-bluff karst country near Maquoketa Caves State Park, from Canton to Joinerville Park in Maquoketa. The 6 miles from Joinerville Park to the Maquoketa City access are not part of the trail, because there is no portage around the Lakehurst power dam. It is a non-meandered stream: the state owns the water, not the bed or the banks, so away from the accesses and public land the shore is private. The DNR maps 6 access sites along it. Of its 5 DNR segments, 2 Intermediate and 3 not yet rated. The DNR's dam layer shows no dam on it. (per Iowa DNR, 2026-10)",
