  blurb:"The Iowa DNR's North Fork and Maquoketa River Water Trail: 31.3 designated miles in Jackson County, designated in June 2023. From the Maquoketa City access past the North Fork confluence at Bridgeport toward the Mississippi. Above the confluence the river is non-meandered; below it the river is meandered, so the bed, banks and sandbars are open to paddlers. The DNR maps 6 access sites along it. The DNR has not yet rated the skill level of its 7 segments. The DNR's dam layer shows no dam on it. (per Iowa DNR, 2026-10)",
