  blurb:"The Iowa DNR's North Fork and Maquoketa River Water Trail: 27.8 designated miles in Jackson County, designated in June 2023. Wild country along the Ozark Wildlife Area, with rapids below the Highway 61 bridge near mile 8 that the DNR calls a challenge. It is a non-meandered stream: the state owns the water, not the bed or the banks, so away from the accesses and public land the shore is private. The DNR maps 1 access site along it. The DNR rates both of its segments Advanced. The DNR's dam layer shows no dam on it. (per Iowa DNR, 2026-10)",
