  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"The Iowa DNR's Middle River Water Trail: 58.0 designated miles in Madison and Adair Counties, designated in October 2011. Dozens of rocky riffles and the Roseman and Holliwell covered bridges of Madison County; the DNR says it is not for beginners, and electric fences may cross the upper reaches. It is a non-meandered stream: the state owns the water, not the bed or the banks, so away from the accesses and public land the shore is private. The DNR maps 6 access sites along it. Of its 8 DNR segments, 7 Intermediate and 1 not yet rated. The DNR's dam layer shows 1 dam on it (Pammel Park Ford). (per Iowa DNR, 2026-10)",
