  waterTrail:{name:"West Fork of the Des Moines River Water Trail", src:"Iowa DNR", designated:"2021-06-23", counties:["Emmet"], miles:31.2, url:"https://www.iowadnr.gov/media/8900/download?inline"},
  geom:"iawt",   // the Iowa DNR's water-trail line (iowa/watertrails) — never snapped or refined
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"The Iowa DNR's West Fork of the Des Moines River Water Trail: 31.2 designated miles in Emmet County, designated in June 2021. A sinuous river across the glacial Des Moines Lobe, wild-feeling north of Estherville and through the 4-Mile Lake wetlands and Anderson Prairie State Preserve. It is non-meandered, so in places the right is only to float on the water. The DNR maps 9 access sites along it, 1 of them fishing accesses rather than ramps. Of its 4 DNR segments, 3 Intermediate and 1 Advanced. The DNR's dam layer shows 1 dam on it (South Riverside Park Dam). (per Iowa DNR, 2026-10)",
