  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 5 entries, tap to read</summary><b>Inland Trout Stream Special Regulations</b><br>• From the Delaware/Sullivan County line downstream of Roscoe upstream to the Route 206 Bridge — SE (pp. 47, 49)<br>• From the downstream end of the Beaver Kill Campground upstream to 0.5 miles upstream of the Beaver Kill covered bridge at the Beaver Kill Campground — SE (p. 47)<br>• From 1.6 miles downstream of Iron Bridge at Horton upstream to 1 mile upstream of Iron Bridge at Horton. — CR. Restrictions: Angling prohibited from July 1 through August 31 from Iron Bridge at Horton downstream to first Route 17 overpass. (p. 49)<br>• From 1 mile upstream of Iron Bridge at Horton upstream to the old railroad trestle 2.5 miles downstream of the Sullivan County Line — SE (p. 49)<br>• From the Sullivan County Line downstream of Roscoe downstream 2.5 miles to the old railroad trestle — CR (p. 49)<br><i>The categories' rules (p. 47):</i><br>Stocked-Extended (SE) and Wild Quality (WQ Categories) — Regulations: April 1–Oct 15, Daily Limit-3 with no more than 1 longer than 12” · Oct 16–Mar 31, Catch and Release only, Artificial lures only<br>Catch and Release (CR Category) — Regulations: All year, Catch and Release only, Artificial lures only<br><br><b>DEC's reach-by-reach rules</b> (NYSDEC Inland Trout Stream Fishing map)<br><i>Trout, April 1 - October 15, Daily Limit - 3 with no more than 1 longer than 12″<br>Trout, October 16 - March 31, Catch and Release only, Artificial Lures only</i><br>• From the downstream end of the Beaver Kill Campground upstream to 0.5 mile upstream of the Beaver Kill covered bridge at the Beaver Kill Campground (Stocked-Extended)<br>• From the Delaware/Sullivan County line downstream of Roscoe upstream to the Route 206 Bridge (Stocked-Extended)<br>• From 1 mile upstream of Iron Bridge at Horton upstream to the old railroad trestle 2.5 miles downstream of the Sullivan County Line (Stocked-Extended)<br><i>Trout, All Year, Catch and Release only, Artificial Lures only</i><br>• From 1.6 miles downstream of Iron Bridge at Horton upstream to 1 mile upstream of Iron Bridge at Horton (Stocked-Extended)<br>• From the Sullivan County Line downstream of Roscoe downstream 2.5 mi to the old railroad trestle (Stocked-Extended)</details><br><br><b>Statewide: Inland Trout Streams</b> (pp. 4–5, 47)<br>Trout stream reaches categorized as Wild or Stocked are managed using statewide inland trout stream regulations (page 4). (p. 47)<br>• Brook, Brown, and Rainbow Trout and Splake in Inland Trout Streams⁴: April 1–Oct 15 · Minimum length: None · Daily limit: 5 with only 2 longer than 12\"<br>• Oct 16–Mar 31: Catch and Release only, Artificial lures only<br>• A person may not fish for a species (not even catch and release) outside of the open season for that species on a given water. (p. 4)<br><i>Inland Trout Streams shall mean all rivers and streams inhabited by trout except as follows:</i><br>• Great Lakes tributaries to the first impassable barrier;<br>• Finger Lakes tributaries to the first impassable barrier;<br>• Lake Champlain tributaries to the first impassable barrier; or<br>• Tidal stream reaches. (p. 5)",
