  parkRegsSrc:"nydec",
  parkRegs:"<b>Region 6 Special Regulations</b><br>• <i>Black River from upstream tip of lowermost island upstream to Mill Street in Watertown</i>: See Great Lakes Regulations (Page 60) (p. 35)<br><br><i>The guide also names this river in its Great Lakes and Tributaries Regulations (pp. 63–65), which apply to Lake Ontario tributaries up to the first impassable barrier.</i><br><br><b>Statewide: Inland Trout Streams</b> (pp. 4–5, 47)<br>Trout stream reaches categorized as Wild or Stocked are managed using statewide inland trout stream regulations (page 4). (p. 47)<br>• Brook, Brown, and Rainbow Trout and Splake in Inland Trout Streams⁴: April 1–Oct 15 · Minimum length: None · Daily limit: 5 with only 2 longer than 12\"<br>• Oct 16–Mar 31: Catch and Release only, Artificial lures only<br>• A person may not fish for a species (not even catch and release) outside of the open season for that species on a given water. (p. 4)<br><i>Inland Trout Streams shall mean all rivers and streams inhabited by trout except as follows:</i><br>• Great Lakes tributaries to the first impassable barrier;<br>• Finger Lakes tributaries to the first impassable barrier;<br>• Lake Champlain tributaries to the first impassable barrier; or<br>• Tidal stream reaches. (p. 5)<br><br><i>DEC's map gives these reaches the statewide rule:</i><br><i>Trout, April 1 - October 15, Daily Limit - 5 with no more than 2 longer than 12\"<br>Trout, October 16 - March 31, Catch and Release only, Artificial Lures only</i><br>• From the Dam in Lyons Falls upstream to 400 yards upstream of Hawkinsville Road (Stocked)<br>• From Factory Square Park upstream to the Route 3 accessable platform (Stocked)<br>• From confluence with Unnamed Tributary 1.2 miles downstream of Dam in Forestport upstream to Dam in Forestport (Stocked)<br>• From 1.3 Miles downstream of Edmunds Road upstream to 1.0 mile upstream of Edmunds Road (Stocked)",
