  parkRegsSrc:"vdwr",
  parkRegs:"<i>No entry of its own in the 2026 Freshwater Fishing &amp; Boating in Virginia: the statewide rules apply.</i><br><br><b>Trout: statewide season and limits</b> (p. 29)<br>Virginia’s trout season is open year-round and the general statewide limits are 6 trout per day, no fish less than 7 inches. There are a number of exceptions found below for certain areas and waters (i.e., heritage, urban, special area, special regulation, and fee fishing waters), so please study the sections following for fishing times, dates, and limits. These different restrictions have been applied to certain wild trout waters, as well as several types of stocked trout streams, to provide anglers with the opportunity to catch more and larger trout.",
