  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 5 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>ANDROSCOGGIN RIVER, Gilead to Brunswick (South Zone)</b> (p. 8)<br>General fishing laws apply, except: Open to open water fishing from the Maine-New Hampshire Border to tidewater from January 1 - December 31.<br>– From the Maine-New Hampshire border downriver to the bridge crossing in Gilead: Single hook artificial lures only. S-7.<br>– From the bridge crossing in Gilead to the Route 232 Bridge, Rumford Point: From April 1<br>- September 30: ALO. Daily bag limit on trout: 1 fish; minimum length limit on landlocked salmon, rainbow trout, and brown trout: 12 inches. All trout between 16 and 20 inches must be released alive at once. From October 1 - March 31: ALO. All trout and landlocked salmon must be released alive at once.<br>– From the Route 232 Bridge, Rumford Point to Livermore Falls Dam: From April 1 - September 30: S-19; minimum length limit on landlocked salmon, rainbow trout, and brown trout: 12 inches. From October 1 - March 31: ALO. All trout and landlocked salmon must be released alive at once.<br>– From the Livermore Falls Dam to tidewater: S-19. Open to ice fishing. (Gilead to Merrymeeting Bay: See Fish Consumption Advisories on page A-4).<br><br><i>The codes above, from the lawbook's Season and Special Law Codes</i> (inside front cover flap):<br>• ALO: Artificial lures only.<br>• S-7: All trout, landlocked salmon, and togue caught must be released alive at once.<br>• S-19: Daily limit on brook trout (includes splake and Arctic charr): 2 fish.</details><br><br><b>Standard rule (South Zone): General Fishing Laws for Inland Waters</b> (inside front cover flap)<br>• Terminal gear, South Zone:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Use of all legal forms of bait (including live baitfish/smelts), artificial lures, and artificial flies is PERMITTED.<br>• Seasons, rivers, streams, brooks (North and South Zones):<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;From Apr 1 to Aug 15: Open to open water fishing.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;From Aug 16 to Sep 30: Open to open water fishing using artificial lures or flies only. General law length and bag limits apply, except daily bag limit one landlocked salmon and one brook trout.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;From Oct 1 to Mar 31: Closed to all fishing.<br>• Daily bag &amp; possession limits by species · length limits, rivers, streams, brooks:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Brook Trout (includes Splake &amp; Arctic charr): 5 fish · 6 inches minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Brown Trout: 2 fish · 6\" min &amp; 25\" max<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Rainbow Trout: 2 fish · 6 inches minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Landlocked Salmon: 2 fish · 14\" min &amp; 25\" max<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Togue (Lake Trout): 2 fish · 18 inches minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Bass (Largemouth &amp; Smallmouth): South Zone: 2 fish · No minimum length. Only 1 may exceed 14 inches.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Whitefish: 3 fish · None<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Smelts: 2 quarts · None<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Sea-run Atlantic Salmon, Redfin Pickerel, Swamp Darter: Endangered or Threatened Species - No Fishing Permitted<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Striped Bass, Shad, River Herring, American Eel, Sturgeon: See page A-1<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Inland species not listed above: Unlimited · None",
