  parkRegs:"<b>KENNEBAGO RIVER, Seven Ponds Twp to Rangeley (North Zone)</b> (p. 25)<br>General fishing laws apply, except: FFO, S-1, S-17, S-22. From August 16 - September 30: FFO, S-7. Tributaries: FFO, and closed to fishing after August 15.<br>– The Logans, so called, from upper (Mahaney) dam upstream to red markers: Open to open water fishing April 1 - September 30: FFO. Daily limit on trout: 5 fish. Minimum length limit on trout: 6 inches, only 1 may exceed 12 inches.<br>– From lower (Kennebago Falls) dam downstream to the red marker at the confluence of Cupsuptic Lake: S-3.<br>– That section of river in Lower Cupsuptic Twp known as the spawning beds approximately 200 yards long between red markers: Closed to fishing after September 15.<br><br><i>The codes above, from the lawbook's Season and Special Law Codes</i> (inside front cover flap):<br>• FFO: Fly fishing only.<br>• S-1: Closed to the taking of smelts.<br>• S-3: Direct tributaries closed to the taking of smelts.<br>• S-7: All trout, landlocked salmon, and togue caught must be released alive at once.<br>• S-17: Daily bag limit on brook trout (includes splake and Arctic charr): 2 fish; minimum length limit: 10 inches, only 1 may exceed 12 inches.<br>• S-22: Daily bag limit on landlocked salmon: 1 fish.<br><br><b>Standard rule (North Zone): General Fishing Laws for Inland Waters</b> (inside front cover flap)<br>• Terminal gear, North Zone:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Use or possession of live fish as bait is PROHIBITED. The use of all other legal forms of bait (including worms and dead baitfish/smelts), artificial lures, and artificial flies is PERMITTED.<br>• Seasons, rivers, streams, brooks (North and South Zones):<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;From Apr 1 to Aug 15: Open to open water fishing.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;From Aug 16 to Sep 30: Open to open water fishing using artificial lures or flies only. General law length and bag limits apply, except daily bag limit one landlocked salmon and one brook trout.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;From Oct 1 to Mar 31: Closed to all fishing.<br>• Daily bag &amp; possession limits by species · length limits, rivers, streams, brooks:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Brook Trout (includes Splake &amp; Arctic charr): 5 fish · 6 inches minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Brown Trout: 2 fish · 6\" min &amp; 25\" max<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Rainbow Trout: 2 fish · 6 inches minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Landlocked Salmon: 2 fish · 14\" min &amp; 25\" max<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Togue (Lake Trout): 2 fish · 18 inches minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Bass (Largemouth &amp; Smallmouth): North Zone: Unlimited · None<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Whitefish: 3 fish · None<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Smelts: 2 quarts · None<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Sea-run Atlantic Salmon, Redfin Pickerel, Swamp Darter: Endangered or Threatened Species - No Fishing Permitted<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Striped Bass, Shad, River Herring, American Eel, Sturgeon: See page A-1<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Inland species not listed above: Unlimited · None",
