  blurb:"59.8 miles in Maine, drawn from USGS National Hydrography Dataset flowlines. The line stops at each lake's shore (a gap in it is still water): East Branch Deadwater, Third Lake and Grand Lake Matagamon. In the North Zone of the 2026 Maine Fishing Laws (59.5 miles), the rest in the South Zone (0.4). The gauge is dam-controlled: below the Grand Lake Matagamon dam this reading is mostly the release.",
