  geom:"nhd",   // NHD flowlines clipped to Maine, lakes cut out (a gap is still water) -- never re-snap
  parkRegsSrc:"maine",
  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 8 reaches, tap to read</summary><b>ALLAGASH RIVER, T10 R12 WELS to Allagash (North Zone)</b> (p. 7)<br>General fishing laws apply, except:<br>– From Churchill Dam downstream to the red markers at the confluence of Chisholm Brook, T10 R12 WELS. Fishing is prohibited in or from the fishway in Churchill Dam; there are no distance restrictions when fishing near the fishway. ALO, S-19. Only one brook trout may exceed 14 inches. From August 16 - September 30: ALO. Minimum length limit on brook trout: 12 inches. Total daily bag limit on trout and togue: 1 fish.<br>– From Long Lake Dam downstream to Allagash Falls and all tributaries. From August 16 - September 30: ALO. Total daily bag limit on trout and togue: 1 fish.<br>– From Allagash Falls downstream to the confluence with the St. John River. S-11. Closed to the taking of live baitfish except by hook and line. The general law maximum length limit on landlocked salmon does not apply. From October 1 - November 30: ALO. Open to taking bass and muskellunge only. (See Allagash Wilderness Waterway).<br><br><i>The river's entry ends “(See Allagash Wilderness Waterway)”: the area listing</i><br><b>ALLAGASH WILDERNESS WATERWAY, T6 R11 WELS to Allagash</b> (p. 7)<br>AWW Watercraft Restrictions (Summary):<br>- From the south end of Telos Lake to the north end of Chamberlain Lake, the use of all models of personal watercraft (PWC), hovercraft, airboats, racing boats, and pontoon boats is prohibited.<br>- From Lock Dam Stream, where it enters Eagle Lake north to twin Brook Rapids, only canoes without motors or motors not exceeding 10 hp, may be used on the watercourse.<br>- On Allagash Lake and Allagash entrance of Chamberlain Lake, all watercraft are prohibited except canoes without motors.<br>- Except on Telos and Chamberlain Lakes, the use of inflatable watercraft is prohibited.<br>- Water skiing or other activities in which individuals are towed behind watercraft are prohibited. For a complete copy of regulations or other information on the use of the Allagash Wilderness Waterway, contact: Allagash Wilderness Waterway, c/o Northern Regional Office, 106 Hogan Rd, Suite 7, Bangor, Maine 04401; 207-941-4014; or www.maine.gov/allagash.<br><br><i>The codes above, from the lawbook's Season and Special Law Codes</i> (inside front cover flap):<br>• ALO: Artificial lures only.<br>• S-11: The use or possession of live baitfish/live smelts is permitted.<br>• S-19: Daily limit on brook trout (includes splake and Arctic charr): 2 fish.</details><br><br><b>Standard rule (North Zone): General Fishing Laws for Inland Waters</b> (inside front cover flap)<br>• Terminal gear, North Zone:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Use or possession of live fish as bait is PROHIBITED. The use of all other legal forms of bait (including worms and dead baitfish/smelts), artificial lures, and artificial flies is PERMITTED.<br>• Seasons, rivers, streams, brooks (North and South Zones):<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;From Apr 1 to Aug 15: Open to open water fishing.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;From Aug 16 to Sep 30: Open to open water fishing using artificial lures or flies only. General law length and bag limits apply, except daily bag limit one landlocked salmon and one brook trout.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;From Oct 1 to Mar 31: Closed to all fishing.<br>• Daily bag &amp; possession limits by species · length limits, rivers, streams, brooks:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Brook Trout (includes Splake &amp; Arctic charr): 5 fish · 6 inches minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Brown Trout: 2 fish · 6\" min &amp; 25\" max<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Rainbow Trout: 2 fish · 6 inches minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Landlocked Salmon: 2 fish · 14\" min &amp; 25\" max<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Togue (Lake Trout): 2 fish · 18 inches minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Bass (Largemouth &amp; Smallmouth): North Zone: Unlimited · None<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Whitefish: 3 fish · None<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Smelts: 2 quarts · None<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Sea-run Atlantic Salmon, Redfin Pickerel, Swamp Darter: Endangered or Threatened Species - No Fishing Permitted<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Striped Bass, Shad, River Herring, American Eel, Sturgeon: See page A-1<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;Inland species not listed above: Unlimited · None",
