  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 5 reaches, tap to read</summary><i>Trout Fishing (p. 24):</i> Missouri has several types of trout fishing areas, each with its own special rules. In addition to a fishing permit, you will need a trout permit to possess trout on all waters outside of the trout parks and a daily tag while fishing in the trout parks. Unless otherwise indicated, the season is open all year.<br><br><b>Trout Park: Montauk State Park</b> (p. 24)<br>Maramec Spring Park, Bennett Spring State Park, Montauk State Park, and Roaring River State Park are open and stocked daily from March 1 through Oct. 31. Anglers need a fishing permit, unless exempt, as well as a daily trout tag. The price for a daily trout tag is $5 for anglers 16 and older, and $3 for anglers 15 and younger. Note: At Roaring River State Park, a daily tag or a trout permit may be used for fishing from the first bridge below the old dam in Zone 3 to the downstream park boundary.<br>The daily limit is 4 rainbow or brown trout in the aggregate. The possession limit is 8 trout in the aggregate statewide. You must stop fishing for any species after having the daily limit of trout in possession. Area regulations, fishing methods, and zones vary. Ask for details when you purchase your daily trout tag.<br><i>Winter Fishing at the Trout Parks (p. 24):</i> Only catch-and-release fishing is available from Nov. 13, 2026 through Feb. 8, 2027. Maramec Spring Park is open daily from 8 a.m. to 4 p.m. The three state parks are open from 8 a.m. to 4 p.m. on Friday through Monday. A fishing permit, unless exempt, and a trout permit are required. Only flies may be used.<br><i>Porous-Soled Waders (p. 24):</i> To prevent the spread of an invasive algae called didymo, the use of shoes, boots, or waders with porous soles of felt, matted, or woven fibrous material is prohibited at all trout parks and where specified on pages 26–35.<br><br><b>Current River</b> (p. 31)<br><i>Mainstem and its tributaries:</i><br>• Walleye and sauger — 18\" minimum length limit<br><i>In Dent, Texas, and Shannon counties:</i><br>• The use of porous-soled waders is prohibited. See Page 24.<br><i>From Montauk State Park to the river crossing on Dent County Road 6510/Shannon County Big Creek Road at Cedargrove:</i><br>• Blue Ribbon Trout Area — See Page 26 for special regulations.<br>• Only flies and artificial lures may be used, and soft plastic baits and natural and scented baits are prohibited when fishing for any species.<br>• Gigging, bowfishing, and using an atlatl are prohibited, and fish taken by these methods may not be possessed on these waters or their banks.<br><i>From the river crossing on Dent County Road 6510/Shannon County Big Creek Road at Cedargrove to the Arkansas line:</i><br>• Nongame fish — The daily limit may include no more than 5 hog suckers.</details><br><br><b>Statewide: Game Fish Seasons and Limits</b> (p. 20)<br>• Trout · Open Season: All year · Daily Limit: 4<sup>1</sup> · Length Limit: Rainbow: none<sup>1</sup>; Brown: 15\" minimum in streams<br>• Black bass (largemouth, smallmouth, spotted/Kentucky) · Daily Limit: 6<sup>1</sup><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;– From impoundments · Open Season: All year · Length Limit: None<sup>1</sup><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;– From most streams south of the Missouri River<sup>2</sup> · Open Season: May 23, 2026–Feb. 28, 2027 · Length Limit: 12\" minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;– From other streams<sup>2</sup> · Open Season: All year · Length Limit: 12\" minimum<br><sup>1</sup> Applies on all waters, with the exception of those with more specific regulations found on pages 24–35 and on areas that are posted with special regulations.<br><sup>2</sup> Black bass fishing and possession is open year-round on the Mississippi River, all waters north of the south bank of the Missouri River, the St. Francis River downstream from Wappapello Dam, and on streams in that portion of southeast Missouri bounded by a line from Cape Girardeau following Missouri highways 74 and 25, U.S. highways 60, 67, and 160, and the west bank of the Little Black River to the Arkansas state line. In the rest of the state, black bass from streams may not be possessed from March 1–May 22, 2026. Only catch-and-release fishing for black bass is allowed during this time in this area of the state.<br><br><b>Statewide: Nongame Fish Seasons and Limits</b> (p. 21)<br>• Gig, atlatl · Season: Sept. 15–Feb. 15 · Time: Sunrise to midnight · Location: Streams and impounded waters<br><i>Daily limits, and every other method, are in that table on p. 21.</i>",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"Montauk State Park holds one of Missouri’s four trout parks, which MDC keeps “open and stocked daily from March 1 through Oct. 31”; from Nov. 13, 2026 through Feb. 8, 2027 it is catch-and-release with flies only, 8 a.m. to 4 p.m. on Friday through Monday (2026 Summary, p. 24). MDC lists it in Dent County.",
  fish:"rainbow and brown trout (trout park, stocked daily March 1–Oct. 31)",
