  troutClass:"mo_taneycomo", reachClass:["mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo","mo_taneycomo"], troutSource:"mdc",
  parkRegsSrc:"mdc",
  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 6 reaches, tap to read</summary><i>Trout Fishing (p. 24):</i> Missouri has several types of trout fishing areas, each with its own special rules. In addition to a fishing permit, you will need a trout permit to possess trout on all waters outside of the trout parks and a daily tag while fishing in the trout parks. Unless otherwise indicated, the season is open all year.<br><br><b>Lake Taneycomo and its tributaries</b><sup>1,2,3,4</sup> (p. 26)<br>Directions and total miles: From the closed zone 760 feet below Table Rock Dam to the mouth of Fall Creek — 3 miles<br>• County: Taney · Length Limit: Rainbows: less than 12\" or greater than 20\"; Browns: at least 20\" · Daily Limit: 4 (only 1 brown) · Authorized Lures: Artificial lures and flies<br><br><b>Lake Taneycomo</b><sup>1,2,3,4</sup> (p. 27)<br>Directions and total miles: Mouth of Fall Creek to Powersite Dam and tributaries to Lake Taneycomo — 19.7 miles<br>• County: Taney · Length Limit: Rainbows: none; Browns: at least 20\" · Daily Limit: 4 (only 1 brown) · Authorized Lures: All<br><br><i>Notes to the table (p. 27):</i><br><sup>1</sup> The use of porous-soled waders is prohibited. See Page 24.<br><sup>2</sup> While on any waters with length limits, all trout you possess must be kept with head, tail, and skin intact.<br><sup>3</sup> Lake Taneycomo is stocked monthly with rainbow trout and annually with brown trout.<br><sup>4</sup> Must also have trout permit upstream of U.S. Highway 65 bridge to fish for any species.<br><br><i>Porous-Soled Waders (p. 24):</i> To prevent the spread of an invasive algae called didymo, the use of shoes, boots, or waders with porous soles of felt, matted, or woven fibrous material is prohibited at all trout parks and where specified on pages 26–35.<br><br><b>Lake Taneycomo</b> (p. 28)<br><i>On the lake and its tributaries:</i><br>• Brown trout — 20\" minimum length limit; the daily limit of 4 trout, combined total of both species, may include only 1 brown trout.<br>• The use of porous-soled waders is prohibited. See Page 24.<br><i>Within 760 feet below Table Rock Dam:</i><br>• No fishing is allowed.<br><i>From the closed zone 760 feet below Table Rock Dam to the mouth of Fall Creek:</i><br>• Rainbow trout — 12\" to 20\" protected slot length limit<br>• Pole and line fishing only<br>• Only flies and artificial lures may be used, and soft plastic baits and natural and scented baits are prohibited when fishing for any species.<br><i>From the closed zone 760 feet below Table Rock Dam to U.S. Highway 65 bridge:</i><br>• Fishing permit (unless exempt) and a trout permit are required to fish for any species.</details><br><br><b>Statewide: Game Fish Seasons and Limits</b> (p. 20)<br>• Trout · Open Season: All year · Daily Limit: 4<sup>1</sup> · Length Limit: Rainbow: none<sup>1</sup>; Brown: 15\" minimum in streams<br>• Black bass (largemouth, smallmouth, spotted/Kentucky) · Daily Limit: 6<sup>1</sup><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;– From impoundments · Open Season: All year · Length Limit: None<sup>1</sup><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;– From most streams south of the Missouri River<sup>2</sup> · Open Season: May 23, 2026–Feb. 28, 2027 · Length Limit: 12\" minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;– From other streams<sup>2</sup> · Open Season: All year · Length Limit: 12\" minimum<br><sup>1</sup> Applies on all waters, with the exception of those with more specific regulations found on pages 24–35 and on areas that are posted with special regulations.<br><sup>2</sup> Black bass fishing and possession is open year-round on the Mississippi River, all waters north of the south bank of the Missouri River, the St. Francis River downstream from Wappapello Dam, and on streams in that portion of southeast Missouri bounded by a line from Cape Girardeau following Missouri highways 74 and 25, U.S. highways 60, 67, and 160, and the west bank of the Little Black River to the Arkansas state line. In the rest of the state, black bass from streams may not be possessed from March 1–May 22, 2026. Only catch-and-release fishing for black bass is allowed during this time in this area of the state.<br><br><b>Statewide: Nongame Fish Seasons and Limits</b> (p. 21)<br>• Gig, atlatl · Season: Sept. 15–Feb. 15 · Time: Sunrise to midnight · Location: Streams and impounded waters<br><i>Daily limits, and every other method, are in that table on p. 21.</i>",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"MDC manages Lake Taneycomo as trout water: a trout area (from the closed zone 760 feet below Table Rock Dam to the mouth of Fall Creek, 3 miles, Taney County); a trout area (mouth of Fall Creek to Powersite Dam and tributaries to Lake Taneycomo, 19.7 miles, Taney County) (2026 Summary, pp. 26–27). MDC says “Lake Taneycomo is stocked monthly with rainbow trout and annually with brown trout” (p. 27).",
  fish:"rainbow trout (stocked monthly) and brown trout (stocked annually) (p. 27)",
