  id:"bourbeusemo", name:"Bourbeuse River", color:"#1f6f8b",
  state:"MO", region:"missouri", gauges:["bourbeuseHigh","bourbeuseUnion"], primaryGauge:"bourbeuseUnion",
  geom:"osm", osmName:"Bourbeuse River",
  parkRegsSrc:"mdc",
  parkRegs:"<b>Bourbeuse River</b> (p. 30)<br><i>Mainstem and its tributaries:</i><br>• Black bass — The daily and possession limit is 12 fish and may include no more than 6 largemouth bass and smallmouth bass, combined total of both species.<br>• Spotted bass — No minimum length limit<br><br><b>Statewide: Game Fish Seasons and Limits</b> (p. 20)<br>• Trout · Open Season: All year · Daily Limit: 4<sup>1</sup> · Length Limit: Rainbow: none<sup>1</sup>; Brown: 15\" minimum in streams<br>• Black bass (largemouth, smallmouth, spotted/Kentucky) · Daily Limit: 6<sup>1</sup><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;– From impoundments · Open Season: All year · Length Limit: None<sup>1</sup><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;– From most streams south of the Missouri River<sup>2</sup> · Open Season: May 23, 2026–Feb. 28, 2027 · Length Limit: 12\" minimum<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;– From other streams<sup>2</sup> · Open Season: All year · Length Limit: 12\" minimum<br><sup>1</sup> Applies on all waters, with the exception of those with more specific regulations found on pages 24–35 and on areas that are posted with special regulations.<br><sup>2</sup> Black bass fishing and possession is open year-round on the Mississippi River, all waters north of the south bank of the Missouri River, the St. Francis River downstream from Wappapello Dam, and on streams in that portion of southeast Missouri bounded by a line from Cape Girardeau following Missouri highways 74 and 25, U.S. highways 60, 67, and 160, and the west bank of the Little Black River to the Arkansas state line. In the rest of the state, black bass from streams may not be possessed from March 1–May 22, 2026. Only catch-and-release fishing for black bass is allowed during this time in this area of the state.<br><br><b>Statewide: Nongame Fish Seasons and Limits</b> (p. 21)<br>• Gig, atlatl · Season: Sept. 15–Feb. 15 · Time: Sunrise to midnight · Location: Streams and impounded waters<br><i>Daily limits, and every other method, are in that table on p. 21.</i>",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
