  parkRegs:"<b>Androscoggin River · Errol · Errol Dam to the markers at the dead water at Bragg Bay</b> (p. 23)<br>Fly-fishing only. Daily limit for trout 2 fish; minimum length 12 inches<br><br><i>The reach runs on to Pontook Dam; the drawn line stops where Pontook Reservoir begins (the reservoir is cut out).</i><br><b>Androscoggin River · Dummer · Dummer-Cambridge town line to Pontook Dam</b> (p. 23)<br>No closed season for all species except salmon. Daily limit of 2 trout through the ice.<br><br><i>The table's own note</i> (pp. 23–25): For species not listed under this section, please refer to the General Regulations section for Rivers and Streams.<br><br><i>Fly-fishing, as the digest defines it</i> (p. 8): Fishing by trolling or casting with only fly rod, fly reel, and fly line combination, to include Tenkara, with an artificial fly or cast of artificial flies attached, and does not include the use of spinning, spincast, and casting rods and reels and lead core lines.<br><br><i>The Androscoggin entry from Wheeler Bay in Dummer to Sawmill Dam in Berlin is below this line's end (listed under elsewhere). (p. 23)</i><br><br><i>The NH-ME interstate waters list counts the Androscoggin above Errol Dam as Umbagog Lake water; this line starts at Errol Dam. (p. 38)</i><br><br><b>Standard rule: General Fishing Rules for Rivers &amp; Streams</b> (p. 22)<br>In general, rivers and streams are CLOSED TO ALL FISHING from Oct. 16 through Dec. 31, unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>Fishing through the ice, from the ice, or from any object supported by the ice is prohibited unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>• Black Bass (Smallmouth Bass &amp; Largemouth Bass): January 1 to May 14 · 2 fish daily limit.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;May 15 to June 15 · Catch and release only. · Artificial lures and flies only.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;June 16 to October 15 · 5 fish daily limit.<br>• Brook Trout, Brown Trout, Rainbow Trout and their hybrids: January 1 to October 15 · 5 fish or 5 pounds daily limit, whichever is reached first; no length limit. · “Trout” include Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Golden, and all their hybrids.<br>• Landlocked Salmon: April 1 to September 30 · 2 fish daily limit, minimum length 15 inches. · Salmon may not be taken in any water body after September 30 and before April 1. Salmon may not be taken through the ice.<br><i>Other species: the table on p. 22.</i><br>In instances where special limits, seasons, and methods of taking are not noted for a particular river or stream, the General Fishing Rules apply. Rivers and Streams with no closed season refer to General Lakes and Ponds for species not listed.<br><i>General Fishing Rules for Lakes and Ponds: p. 12.</i>",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
