  parkRegs:"<i>No entry of its own in the digest's Rivers &amp; Streams with Special Rules (pp. 23–25).</i><br><br><i>This line ends 134 m from Vermont, at the Connecticut River. Its mouth, up to the first highway bridge, is Connecticut River water under the NH–VT interstate rules (p. 39); that bridge was not located on the line.</i><br>For that portion of the river between New Hampshire and Vermont. “Connecticut River” means all waters of the river including the bays, set backs and tributaries, only to the first highway bridge crossing said tributaries on the Vermont and New Hampshire sides.<br><br><b>Standard rule: General Fishing Rules for Rivers &amp; Streams</b> (p. 22)<br>In general, rivers and streams are CLOSED TO ALL FISHING from Oct. 16 through Dec. 31, unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>Fishing through the ice, from the ice, or from any object supported by the ice is prohibited unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>• Black Bass (Smallmouth Bass &amp; Largemouth Bass): January 1 to May 14 · 2 fish daily limit.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;May 15 to June 15 · Catch and release only. · Artificial lures and flies only.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;June 16 to October 15 · 5 fish daily limit.<br>• Brook Trout, Brown Trout, Rainbow Trout and their hybrids: January 1 to October 15 · 5 fish or 5 pounds daily limit, whichever is reached first; no length limit. · “Trout” include Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Golden, and all their hybrids.<br>• Landlocked Salmon: April 1 to September 30 · 2 fish daily limit, minimum length 15 inches. · Salmon may not be taken in any water body after September 30 and before April 1. Salmon may not be taken through the ice.<br><i>Other species: the table on p. 22.</i><br>In instances where special limits, seasons, and methods of taking are not noted for a particular river or stream, the General Fishing Rules apply. Rivers and Streams with no closed season refer to General Lakes and Ponds for species not listed.",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
