  parkRegsSrc:"newhampshire",
  parkRegs:"<i>A closed area at Garvins Falls Dam in Bow, on the drawn line.</i><br><b>Merrimack River · Bow · Garvins Falls Dam from canal wall, including fish bypass plunge pool, to a point 300 feet downstream to main river.</b> (p. 24)<br>Closed to all fishing.<br><br><b>Merrimack River · Franklin to Mass. border (except closed sections) · All sections</b> (p. 24)<br>No closed season for all species except salmon. Daily limit of 2 trout through the ice.<br><br><i>The table's own note</i> (pp. 23–25): For species not listed under this section, please refer to the General Regulations section for Rivers and Streams.<br><br><i>A third Merrimack River entry (Amoskeag Dam to Amoskeag Bridge, Manchester: closed to all fishing) is below this line's end at Hooksett (listed under elsewhere). (p. 24)</i><br><br><b>Standard rule: General Fishing Rules for Rivers &amp; Streams</b> (p. 22)<br>In general, rivers and streams are CLOSED TO ALL FISHING from Oct. 16 through Dec. 31, unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>Fishing through the ice, from the ice, or from any object supported by the ice is prohibited unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>• Black Bass (Smallmouth Bass &amp; Largemouth Bass): January 1 to May 14 · 2 fish daily limit.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;May 15 to June 15 · Catch and release only. · Artificial lures and flies only.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;June 16 to October 15 · 5 fish daily limit.<br>• Brook Trout, Brown Trout, Rainbow Trout and their hybrids: January 1 to October 15 · 5 fish or 5 pounds daily limit, whichever is reached first; no length limit. · “Trout” include Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Golden, and all their hybrids.<br>• Landlocked Salmon: April 1 to September 30 · 2 fish daily limit, minimum length 15 inches. · Salmon may not be taken in any water body after September 30 and before April 1. Salmon may not be taken through the ice.<br><i>Other species: the table on p. 22.</i><br>In instances where special limits, seasons, and methods of taking are not noted for a particular river or stream, the General Fishing Rules apply. Rivers and Streams with no closed season refer to General Lakes and Ponds for species not listed.<br><i>General Fishing Rules for Lakes and Ponds: p. 12.</i>",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
