  blurb:"64.8 miles in New Hampshire, drawn from USGS National Hydrography Dataset flowlines. The line stops at each lake's shore (a gap in it is still water): Mountain Brook Reservoir, Cheshire Pond, Contoocook River Reservoir, Contoocook River Reservoir, an unnamed pond (NHD 135999209) and Powder Mill Pond. Runs through Hopkinton, Peterborough, Henniker, Concord, Bennington, Antrim, Jaffrey, Hillsborough, Deering, Hancock, Boscawen and Greenfield. NH Fish & Game's stocked-streams layer has it stocked in Bennington, Greenfield, Hancock, Henniker, Hillsborough, Jaffrey and Peterborough. Gauge 01085500 sits below Hopkinton Dam, a flood-control dam: in high water it holds flow back.",
