  parkRegs:"<i>Covers part of the drawn line; the reach's ends were not located on it.</i><br><b>Lamprey River · Raymond to Durham · Raymond/Deerfield town line to Wiswall Dam</b> (p. 24)<br>No closed season for all species. Daily limit of 2 trout through the ice.<br><br><i>Covers part of the drawn line; the reach's ends were not located on it.</i><br><b>Lamprey River · Durham · Wiswall Dam to first railroad trestle downstream of Packers Falls</b> (p. 24)<br>No closed season for all species. Oct. 16 to 4th Saturday in April: Catch-and-release, single barbless hook, artificial lures/flies. 4th Saturday in April through Oct. 15: Daily limit for trout 5 fish or 5 lbs. All legal methods.<br><br><b>Lamprey River · Durham · Wiswall Dam area</b> (p. 24)<br>Closed to all fishing 200 feet below Wiswall Dam between April 1 and July 31. Closed to all fishing in the waters 50 feet above the Wiswall Dam year round.<br><br><i>The table's own note</i> (pp. 23–25): For species not listed under this section, please refer to the General Regulations section for Rivers and Streams.<br><br><b>Standard rule: General Fishing Rules for Rivers &amp; Streams</b> (p. 22)<br>In general, rivers and streams are CLOSED TO ALL FISHING from Oct. 16 through Dec. 31, unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>Fishing through the ice, from the ice, or from any object supported by the ice is prohibited unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>• Black Bass (Smallmouth Bass &amp; Largemouth Bass): January 1 to May 14 · 2 fish daily limit.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;May 15 to June 15 · Catch and release only. · Artificial lures and flies only.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;June 16 to October 15 · 5 fish daily limit.<br>• Brook Trout, Brown Trout, Rainbow Trout and their hybrids: January 1 to October 15 · 5 fish or 5 pounds daily limit, whichever is reached first; no length limit. · “Trout” include Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Golden, and all their hybrids.<br>• Landlocked Salmon: April 1 to September 30 · 2 fish daily limit, minimum length 15 inches. · Salmon may not be taken in any water body after September 30 and before April 1. Salmon may not be taken through the ice.<br><i>Other species: the table on p. 22.</i><br>In instances where special limits, seasons, and methods of taking are not noted for a particular river or stream, the General Fishing Rules apply. Rivers and Streams with no closed season refer to General Lakes and Ponds for species not listed.<br><i>General Fishing Rules for Lakes and Ponds: p. 12.</i>",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"54.2 miles in New Hampshire, drawn from USGS National Hydrography Dataset flowlines. The line stops at each lake's shore (a gap in it is still water): an unnamed pond (NHD 141033803), an unnamed pond (NHD 141033954), Freeses Pond and Dead Pond. Runs through Epping, Raymond, Deerfield, Lee, Durham, Newington, Newmarket, Northwood, Greenland and Dover. NH Fish & Game's stocked-streams layer has it stocked in Deerfield, Durham, Epping, Lee, Northwood and Raymond.",
