  parkRegs:"<i>Covers part of the drawn line; the reach's ends were not located on it.</i><br><b>Exeter River · Brentwood to Exeter · Downstream side of the Cross Road bridge to Route 111 bridge</b> (p. 23)<br>No closed season for all species. Oct. 16 to 4th Saturday in April: Catch-and-release, single barbless hook, artificial lures/flies. 4th Saturday in April through Oct. 15: Daily limit for trout 5 fish or 5 lbs. All legal methods.<br><br><i>Covers part of the drawn line; the reach's ends were not located on it.</i><br><b>Exeter River · Sandown to Exeter · From Route 121-A to the Pickpocket Dam and from Route 111 to the Squamscott River</b> (p. 23)<br>No closed season for all species. Daily limit of 2 trout through the ice. Closed to all fishing from the upstream side of the Pickpocket Dam and fishway including a 50 foot radius in front of the fishway on the upstream side to the downstream side of the Cross Road Bridge in the towns of Brentwood and Exeter<br><br><i>The table's own note</i> (pp. 23–25): For species not listed under this section, please refer to the General Regulations section for Rivers and Streams.<br><br><b>Standard rule: General Fishing Rules for Rivers &amp; Streams</b> (p. 22)<br>In general, rivers and streams are CLOSED TO ALL FISHING from Oct. 16 through Dec. 31, unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>Fishing through the ice, from the ice, or from any object supported by the ice is prohibited unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>• Black Bass (Smallmouth Bass &amp; Largemouth Bass): January 1 to May 14 · 2 fish daily limit.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;May 15 to June 15 · Catch and release only. · Artificial lures and flies only.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;June 16 to October 15 · 5 fish daily limit.<br>• Brook Trout, Brown Trout, Rainbow Trout and their hybrids: January 1 to October 15 · 5 fish or 5 pounds daily limit, whichever is reached first; no length limit. · “Trout” include Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Golden, and all their hybrids.<br>• Landlocked Salmon: April 1 to September 30 · 2 fish daily limit, minimum length 15 inches. · Salmon may not be taken in any water body after September 30 and before April 1. Salmon may not be taken through the ice.<br><i>Other species: the table on p. 22.</i><br>In instances where special limits, seasons, and methods of taking are not noted for a particular river or stream, the General Fishing Rules apply. Rivers and Streams with no closed season refer to General Lakes and Ponds for species not listed.<br><i>General Fishing Rules for Lakes and Ponds: p. 12.</i>",
