  parkRegs:"<i>Covers part of the drawn line; the reach's ends were not located on it.</i><br><b>Sugar River · Newport · Rte. 11/103 Bridge to the so-called Oak Street Bridge</b> (p. 25)<br>Jan. 1 – Nov. 30 season. Fly-fishing only. Daily limit for trout is 2 fish.<br><br><i>The table's own note</i> (pp. 23–25): For species not listed under this section, please refer to the General Regulations section for Rivers and Streams.<br><br><i>Fly-fishing, as the digest defines it</i> (p. 8): Fishing by trolling or casting with only fly rod, fly reel, and fly line combination, to include Tenkara, with an artificial fly or cast of artificial flies attached, and does not include the use of spinning, spincast, and casting rods and reels and lead core lines.<br><br><i>This line ends 110 m from Vermont, at the Connecticut River. Its mouth, up to the first highway bridge, is Connecticut River water under the NH–VT interstate rules (p. 39); that bridge was not located on the line.</i><br>For that portion of the river between New Hampshire and Vermont. “Connecticut River” means all waters of the river including the bays, set backs and tributaries, only to the first highway bridge crossing said tributaries on the Vermont and New Hampshire sides.<br><br><b>Standard rule: General Fishing Rules for Rivers &amp; Streams</b> (p. 22)<br>In general, rivers and streams are CLOSED TO ALL FISHING from Oct. 16 through Dec. 31, unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>Fishing through the ice, from the ice, or from any object supported by the ice is prohibited unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>• Black Bass (Smallmouth Bass &amp; Largemouth Bass): January 1 to May 14 · 2 fish daily limit.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;May 15 to June 15 · Catch and release only. · Artificial lures and flies only.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;June 16 to October 15 · 5 fish daily limit.<br>• Brook Trout, Brown Trout, Rainbow Trout and their hybrids: January 1 to October 15 · 5 fish or 5 pounds daily limit, whichever is reached first; no length limit. · “Trout” include Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Golden, and all their hybrids.<br>• Landlocked Salmon: April 1 to September 30 · 2 fish daily limit, minimum length 15 inches. · Salmon may not be taken in any water body after September 30 and before April 1. Salmon may not be taken through the ice.<br><i>Other species: the table on p. 22.</i><br>In instances where special limits, seasons, and methods of taking are not noted for a particular river or stream, the General Fishing Rules apply. Rivers and Streams with no closed season refer to General Lakes and Ponds for species not listed.",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"26.2 miles in New Hampshire, drawn from USGS National Hydrography Dataset flowlines. The line stops at each lake's shore (a gap in it is still water): Sunapee Lake. Runs through Newport, Claremont and Sunapee. NH Fish & Game's stocked-streams layer has it stocked in Claremont, Newport and Sunapee. Gauge 01152010 is lake-controlled: just below the Lake Sunapee outlet dam, this reading is mostly the lake's release.",
