  parkRegsSrc:"newhampshire",
  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 3 entries, tap to read</summary><b>Merrymeeting River · New Durham · Merrymeeting Lake Dam to 200 ft below Powder Mill Hatchery</b> (p. 24)<br>Closed to all fishing<br><br><b>Merrymeeting River · New Durham to Alton · From 200 ft. below Powder Mill Hatchery to lower dam at Alton</b> (p. 24)<br>No closed season for all species except salmon. Daily limit of 2 trout through the ice<br><br><b>Merrymeeting River · Alton · From lower dam at Alton to Route 11 bridge at Alton Bay</b> (p. 24)<br>Jan. 1 – June 15 and Oct. 1–31 fly-fishing only, barbless hooks, catch-and-release. June 16 – Sept. 30 combined daily limit for trout and salmon is 2 fish, minimum length 15 inches, minimum length for lake trout 18 inches<br><br><i>The table's own note</i> (pp. 23–25): For species not listed under this section, please refer to the General Regulations section for Rivers and Streams.<br><br><i>Fly-fishing, as the digest defines it</i> (p. 8): Fishing by trolling or casting with only fly rod, fly reel, and fly line combination, to include Tenkara, with an artificial fly or cast of artificial flies attached, and does not include the use of spinning, spincast, and casting rods and reels and lead core lines.<br><br><i>Lakes &amp; Ponds with Special Rules: the Lake Winnipesaukee row names the lake areas within 500 feet of the Merrymeeting River among others. That is lake water, below this line's end at the Route 11 bridge. (p. 19)</i></details><br><br><b>Standard rule: General Fishing Rules for Rivers &amp; Streams</b> (p. 22)<br>In general, rivers and streams are CLOSED TO ALL FISHING from Oct. 16 through Dec. 31, unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>Fishing through the ice, from the ice, or from any object supported by the ice is prohibited unless specified for a particular river in the Rivers and Streams with Special Rules section.<br>• Black Bass (Smallmouth Bass &amp; Largemouth Bass): January 1 to May 14 · 2 fish daily limit.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;May 15 to June 15 · Catch and release only. · Artificial lures and flies only.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;June 16 to October 15 · 5 fish daily limit.<br>• Brook Trout, Brown Trout, Rainbow Trout and their hybrids: January 1 to October 15 · 5 fish or 5 pounds daily limit, whichever is reached first; no length limit. · “Trout” include Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Golden, and all their hybrids.<br>• Landlocked Salmon: April 1 to September 30 · 2 fish daily limit, minimum length 15 inches. · Salmon may not be taken in any water body after September 30 and before April 1. Salmon may not be taken through the ice.<br><i>Other species: the table on p. 22.</i><br>In instances where special limits, seasons, and methods of taking are not noted for a particular river or stream, the General Fishing Rules apply. Rivers and Streams with no closed season refer to General Lakes and Ponds for species not listed.<br><i>General Fishing Rules for Lakes and Ponds: p. 12.</i>",
