  parkRegsSrc:"wvdnr",
  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 4 booklet entries, tap to read</summary><b>Trout: Special regulation areas — FLY FISHING ONLY</b> (p. 5)<br><i>Second Creek – Greenbrier and Monroe counties</i><br>Marked 2.4-mile section on the Monroe/Greenbrier county line at Rodgers Mill.<br><br><b>Trout: Special regulation areas — FLY FISHING ONLY — rules</b> (p. 5)<br>For waters listed below<br>• Fishing permitted during daylight hours only.<br>• Only artificial flies and streamers may be used or in possession on any of the fly fishing-only streams.<br>• Only conventional fly fishing tackle may be used.<br>• Open-face and closed-face spinning or spincast reels are prohibited.<br>• All fish caught must be returned to water at once.<br>• No trout shall be in the angler’s possession while on stream sections designated as fly-fishing-only streams.<br>• No lure or fly with any scent, oil, or edible enticement added onto, or impregnated into (regardless if the scent is added in the manufacturing process or applied afterward), may be used or possessed on any fly-fishing-only trout stream.<br>• Powerbait, Gulp and other manufactured scented baits are considered illegal under this section and may not be used or possessed on catch-and-release streams.<br><br><b>Trout stocking – Streams</b> (p. 7)<br>• Second Creek (C &amp; R) — Greenbrier, Monroe County — code V<br><br><b>Trout stocking: codes</b> (p. 6)<br>• V: Varies … Varies<br>Updated daily during Trout Stocking Season: Hunting and Fishing Hotline (304) 558-3399 and online at WVdnr.gov</details><br><br><b>Statewide: Regulations Summary — TROUT</b> (p. 1)<br>• TROUT (Rainbow, Golden Rainbow, Brook, Tiger and Brown): Daily Creel Limit 6* (in any combination); Minimum Size None; Possession Limit 12* (in any combination)<br>Jennings Randolph Lake: See Maryland Fishing Regulations. See Trout on pages 4-5 for additional regulations.<br><br><b>Statewide: Other Methods of Fishing</b> (p. 13)<br>IT IS ILLEGAL TO:<br>• fish within 200 feet of Division of Natural Resources personnel who are stocking fish in public waters.",
