  parkRegs:"<b>Other Special Regulations: Baitfish Regulations</b> (p. 10)<br>Zero possession limit for all non-game fishes (including their collection for any use); and no fish, including dead/packaged minnows, may be used as bait in the following waters:<br>• B. Gauley River upstream of the Route 55/20 bridge (i.e., Curtin, W.Va.) including the Cherry, Williams, Cranberry, and upper Gauley rivers and all respective tributaries.<br>NOTE: These areas are delineated on the maps above.<br><br><b>Trout stocking – Streams</b> (p. 7)<br>• South Fork of Cherry River — Greenbrier, Nicholas County — code BW<br><br><b>Trout stocking: codes</b> (p. 6)<br>• BW: Two each month … February – April; One … May<br>Updated daily during Trout Stocking Season: Hunting and Fishing Hotline (304) 558-3399 and online at WVdnr.gov<br><br><b>Statewide: Regulations Summary — TROUT</b> (p. 1)<br>• TROUT (Rainbow, Golden Rainbow, Brook, Tiger and Brown): Daily Creel Limit 6* (in any combination); Minimum Size None; Possession Limit 12* (in any combination)<br>Jennings Randolph Lake: See Maryland Fishing Regulations. See Trout on pages 4-5 for additional regulations.<br><br><b>Statewide: Other Methods of Fishing</b> (p. 13)<br>IT IS ILLEGAL TO:<br>• fish within 200 feet of Division of Natural Resources personnel who are stocking fish in public waters.",
