  parkRegs:"<b>Trout: Special regulation areas — DELAYED HARVEST STREAMS</b> (p. 5)<br><i>Shavers Fork River - Randolph County</i><br>The 5.5-mile section extending from the mouth of Whitmeadow Run downstream to the mouth of McGee Run.<br><br><b>Trout: Special regulation areas — DELAYED HARVEST STREAMS — rules</b> (p. 5)<br>For waters listed below<br>• Catch-and-release regulations apply: November 1 – May 15.<br>• General regulations apply: May 16 – October 31.<br><br><b>Trout stocking – Streams</b> (p. 7)<br>• Shavers Fork (Delayed Harvest) — Randolph County — code V<br>• Shavers Fork (Rail) — Randolph County — code V<br>• Shavers Fork (Lower Section) — Randolph County — code W-F<br>• Shavers Fork (Upper Section) — Randolph County — code W-F<br><br><b>Trout stocking: codes</b> (p. 6)<br>• F: One ... each week for two weeks, beginning on the third Monday of October<br>• V: Varies … Varies<br>• W: One … January; Two … February; One each week … March – May<br>Updated daily during Trout Stocking Season: Hunting and Fishing Hotline (304) 558-3399 and online at WVdnr.gov<br><br><b>Statewide: Regulations Summary — TROUT</b> (p. 1)<br>• TROUT (Rainbow, Golden Rainbow, Brook, Tiger and Brown): Daily Creel Limit 6* (in any combination); Minimum Size None; Possession Limit 12* (in any combination)<br>Jennings Randolph Lake: See Maryland Fishing Regulations. See Trout on pages 4-5 for additional regulations.<br><br><b>Statewide: Other Methods of Fishing</b> (p. 13)<br>IT IS ILLEGAL TO:<br>• fish within 200 feet of Division of Natural Resources personnel who are stocking fish in public waters.",
