  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 1 entry, tap to read</summary><b>Farmington River/West Branch Farmington River, Hartland-Windsor</b> (p. 44)<br><b>Seasonal Catch and Release Trout Management Area: Hogback Dam (Hartland) to old abutments (Barkhamsted).</b> <b>Trout</b>:<br>September 1 until 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April, catch and release only. From 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April until August 31, daily limit 2 fish, 12-inch minimum length.<br><b>Year-Round Catch and Release Trout Management Area: Old bridge abutments (Barkhamsted) to Route 219 (New Hartford).</b><br><b>Trout:</b> Catch and release year-round. Barbless hooks required.<br><b>Seasonal Catch and Release Trout Management Area: Route 219 (New Hartford) to Route 177 (Farmington).</b> <b>Trout</b>: September 1 until 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April, catch and release only. From 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April until August 31, daily limit 2 fish, 12-inch minimum length.<br><b>Route 177 (Farmington) to Rainbow Reservoir (Windsor Locks).</b> <b>Trout</b>: March 1 until 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April, catch and release only. From 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April until the last day of February, daily limit 5 fish.<br><b>Tidal Waters and Tributaries:</b> The confluence with Rainbow Brook (confluence of the tail race canal and the spillway channel) downstream to the CT River<br><b>Trout</b>:<br><b>Min. Length:</b> 15-inches, harvest allowed year-round.<br><b>Daily limit:</b> 2<br><b>Trophy Common Carp Water:</b> <b>Common Carp</b> <b>Maximum Length:</b> 26-inches<br><b>Daily limit:</b> 2 carp <i>Note: All fishing is prohibited from the confluence with Rainbow Brook UPSTREAM to the Rainbow Dam in either the tail race canal and the spillway channel.</i></details><br><br><i>The guide's summary of these categories:</i><br>• Year-round catch and release fishing only: … A trout and salmon stamp is required to fish in these waters. (p. 39)<br>• Seasonal Harvest: Catch and release fishing only from September 1 to 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April. Harvest allowed from 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April until August 31. A trout and salmon stamp is required to fish in these waters. (p. 39)<br>• Tidal Waters and Tributaries: Sections of these waters where trout harvest is allowed year-round. Special rules apply to for some species in these sections. Daily limit is 2 trout, 15-inch minimum length. (p. 40)<br><br><b>Statewide: Default Species Regulations for Waters of the Inland District</b> (pp. 9, 11, 42)<br>Statewide regulations apply to the sections of rivers or streams which are outside of the areas described for each waterbody in this section. (p. 42)<br>The following regulations are in effect for all waters without a special regulation. (p. 9)<br><i>Trout (Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Tiger, Lake)</i><br>• Min. Length: 9 inches<br>• Daily Limit: 5<br>• Methods: Angling, Ice Fishing<br>• Season: Year-round*<br>*Catch and Release only from March 1 until 6:00am on the second Saturday of April.<br>A Trout and Salmon Stamp is required to keep trout or salmon. (p. 11)",
