  troutClass:"ct_wild1", reachClass:["ct_wild1","ct_tma"], troutSource:"ctdeep",
  parkRegsSrc:"ctdeep",
  parkRegs:"<b>Mill River, Fairfield</b> (p. 48)<br><b>Wild Trout Management Area Class 1:</b> The confluence with Canoe Brook, as posted with signs by CT DEEP, downstream to the crossing with the Merritt Parkway.<br><b>Trout</b>: Catch and release year-round.<br>Gear limited to an artificial lure/fly with single barbless hook.<br><b>Year-Round Catch and Release Trout Management Area:</b> Merritt Parkway crossing downstream to Lake Mohegan (Fairfield).<br><b>Trout</b>: Catch and Release year-round.<br><br><i>The guide's summary of these categories:</i><br>• Year-round catch and release fishing only: … A trout and salmon stamp is required to fish in these waters. (p. 39)<br>• Class 1: Year-round catch and release fishing only and requires the use of a single barbless hook on an artificial lure or fly. A trout and salmon stamp is required to fish in these waters. (p. 39)<br><br><b>Statewide: Default Species Regulations for Waters of the Inland District</b> (pp. 9, 11, 42)<br>Statewide regulations apply to the sections of rivers or streams which are outside of the areas described for each waterbody in this section. (p. 42)<br>The following regulations are in effect for all waters without a special regulation. (p. 9)<br><i>Trout (Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Tiger, Lake)</i><br>• Min. Length: 9 inches<br>• Daily Limit: 5<br>• Methods: Angling, Ice Fishing<br>• Season: Year-round*<br>*Catch and Release only from March 1 until 6:00am on the second Saturday of April.<br>A Trout and Salmon Stamp is required to keep trout or salmon. (p. 11)",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"1.7 miles drawn from CT DEEP's Fisheries Management Area lines. Wild Trout Management Area (Class 1): “From first bridge (S. Park Ave.) below Easton Res. to downstream of third bridge (S. Park Ave.).” Trout Management Area: “From Merrit Parkway bridge downstream to Mohegan Park Pond.” Regulations from the 2026 Connecticut Fishing Guide.",
