  troutClass:"ct_wild1", troutSource:"ctdeep",
  parkRegsSrc:"ctdeep",
  parkRegs:"<b>Quinnipiac River, Southington-New Haven</b> (p. 50)<br><b>Wild Trout Management Area Class 1:</b> The entire river in Southington and Cheshire upstream of Cheshire Street. <b>Trout</b>: Catch and release year-round. Gear limited to an artificial lure/fly with single barbless hook.<br><b>Tidal Waters and Tributaries:</b> The Route 5 crossing (North Haven) downstream to the New Haven Harbor.<br><b>Trout</b>:<br><b>Min. Length:</b> 15-inches, harvest allowed year-round.<br><b>Daily limit:</b> 2<br><b>Common Carp Enhanced Bow and Arrow Fishing Water:</b> When fishing with bow and arrow <b>Daily Limit:</b> 12 carp, not more than 3 of which can be greater than 30 inches.<br><br><i>The guide's summary of these categories:</i><br>• Class 1: Year-round catch and release fishing only and requires the use of a single barbless hook on an artificial lure or fly. A trout and salmon stamp is required to fish in these waters. (p. 39)<br>• Tidal Waters and Tributaries: Sections of these waters where trout harvest is allowed year-round. Special rules apply to for some species in these sections. Daily limit is 2 trout, 15-inch minimum length. (p. 40)<br><br><b>Statewide: Default Species Regulations for Waters of the Inland District</b> (pp. 9, 11, 42)<br>Statewide regulations apply to the sections of rivers or streams which are outside of the areas described for each waterbody in this section. (p. 42)<br>The following regulations are in effect for all waters without a special regulation. (p. 9)<br><i>Trout (Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Tiger, Lake)</i><br>• Min. Length: 9 inches<br>• Daily Limit: 5<br>• Methods: Angling, Ice Fishing<br>• Season: Year-round*<br>*Catch and Release only from March 1 until 6:00am on the second Saturday of April.<br>A Trout and Salmon Stamp is required to keep trout or salmon. (p. 11)",
