  parkRegs:"<b>Saugatuck River, Westport</b> (p. 52)<br><b>William “Doc” Skerlick Trout Management Area</b> <b>Seasonal Catch and Release Trout Management Area: The Dorrs Mill Dam downstream to the Merritt Parkway crossing.</b><br><b>Trout</b>: September 1 until 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April, catch and release only. From 6:00 am second Saturday of April until August 31, 2 trout daily limit.<br>Gear restricted to fly fishing only.<br><b>Sea-Run Trout Stream:</b> Downstream of the “Wood Dam” (Westport)<br><b>Trout</b>::<br><b>Min. Length:</b> 15-inches, harvest allowed year-round<br><b>Daily limit:</b> 2<br><br><i>The guide's summary of these categories:</i><br>• Seasonal Harvest: Catch and release fishing only from September 1 to 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April. Harvest allowed from 6:00 am on the second Saturday of April until August 31. A trout and salmon stamp is required to fish in these waters. (p. 39)<br>• Sea-Run Trout Streams: Daily limit is 2 trout, 15- inch minimum length. Harvest of trout is allowed year-round. A trout and salmon stamp is required to keep trout. (p. 40)<br><br><b>Statewide: Default Species Regulations for Waters of the Inland District</b> (pp. 9, 11, 42)<br>Statewide regulations apply to the sections of rivers or streams which are outside of the areas described for each waterbody in this section. (p. 42)<br>The following regulations are in effect for all waters without a special regulation. (p. 9)<br><i>Trout (Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Tiger, Lake)</i><br>• Min. Length: 9 inches<br>• Daily Limit: 5<br>• Methods: Angling, Ice Fishing<br>• Season: Year-round*<br>*Catch and Release only from March 1 until 6:00am on the second Saturday of April.<br>A Trout and Salmon Stamp is required to keep trout or salmon. (p. 11)",
