  parkRegs:"<b>Stratton Brook, Simsbury</b> — <i>New in the 2026 guide</i> (p. 52)<br><b>Wild Trout Management Area Class 1:</b> Upstream of the confluence with Hop Brook, except for the impoundment within Stratton Brook State Park, which is a trout park.<br><b>Trout</b>: Catch and release year-round. Gear limited to an artificial lure/fly with single barbless hook.<br><br><i>The guide's summary of this category:</i><br>• Class 1: Year-round catch and release fishing only and requires the use of a single barbless hook on an artificial lure or fly. A trout and salmon stamp is required to fish in these waters. (p. 39)<br><br><b>Statewide: Default Species Regulations for Waters of the Inland District</b> (pp. 9, 11, 42)<br>Statewide regulations apply to the sections of rivers or streams which are outside of the areas described for each waterbody in this section. (p. 42)<br>The following regulations are in effect for all waters without a special regulation. (p. 9)<br><i>Trout (Brook, Brown, Rainbow, Tiger, Lake)</i><br>• Min. Length: 9 inches<br>• Daily Limit: 5<br>• Methods: Angling, Ice Fishing<br>• Season: Year-round*<br>*Catch and Release only from March 1 until 6:00am on the second Saturday of April.<br>A Trout and Salmon Stamp is required to keep trout or salmon. (p. 11)",
