  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 2 entries, tap to read</summary><i>Covers about 32.3 km of the 40.3 km mapped.</i><br><b>Batten Kill River (R-BK) · Arlington/ Sunderland/ Manchester · Bennington</b> (p. 40)<br>From NY state line upstream (20.6 miles) to downstream side of Depot Street bridge (Routes 11/30) in Manchester. (R–BK)<br>• All trout must be released immediately<br>• Closed to fishing from November 1 to the Friday before the second Saturday in April.<br><i>Table</i> 1 · <i>ANS</i> WD<br><br><i>Covers about 8.8 km of the 40.3 km mapped.</i><br><b>Batten Kill River (R-BK) · Manchester and Dorset · Bennington</b> (p. 40)<br>Depot Street bridge (Routes 11/30) in Manchester to downstream side of US Route 7 bridge south of East Dorset. (R–BK)<br>• Trout: Oct. 1–Oct. 31: Catch and Release (includes tributaries: Green River, Roaring Branch, Warm Brook) fishing only, all trout must be released immediately.<br><i>Table</i> 1 · <i>ANS</i> WD<br><br><i>The index's own note</i> (p. 40): Waters listed in this index have special regulations that override the general regulations and must be followed.<br><br><i>Baitfish restricted water, the tag in the reach cell.</i><br>Baitfish Zones: see page 27 for statewide map. Restricted waters: (R-BK)=Batten Kill River; (R-LC)=Lake Champlain; (R-M)=Lake Memphremagog; (R-CT)=Connecticut River (p. 40)<br>Baitfish used or harvested in these waterbodies may NOT be transported to or used in a different waterbody (p. 27)<br><b>Restricted Waters</b> (p. 28)<br>• Batten Kill (R–BK) and its associated tributaries including but not limited to:<br>– Bourn Brook · – Bromley Brook · – Chunks Brook · – Dry Brook · – Green River · – Lye Brook · – Mad Tom Brook · – Mill Brook · – Roaring Branch · – Warm Brook · – West Branch Batten Kill · – White Creek<br><br>1 – Aquatic Nuisance Species (ANS): EW=Eurasian Watermilfoil; WC=Water Chestnut; WD=Whirling Disease (p. 40)</details><br><br><b>Standard rule: Table 1: General Fishing Regulations for Vermont.</b> (p. 54)<br>Waterbody-specific regulations listed in Index of Rivers and Streams or the Index of Lakes and Ponds override the General Regulations<br>Regulations for all waterbodies NOT listed in the Index of Rivers and Streams (page 40) or the Index of Lakes and Ponds (page 48) fall under this table.<br>Note different regulation for River/Stream and Lake/Pond.<br>• Anadromous Atlantic Salmon · All · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> No open season · <i>Minimum length:</i> NA · <i>Daily limit:</i> 0 · <i>Legal methods:</i> None<br>• Brook Trout and Brown Trout and Rainbow Trout · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> None · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of brook + brown + rainbow = no more than 8 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Lake Trout · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 18” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of lake trout + landlocked salmon = no more than 2 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Landlocked Atlantic Salmon · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 17” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of lake trout + landlocked salmon = no more than 2 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Largemouth and Smallmouth Bass · All · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in June to March 15 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 10” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of largemouth + smallmouth = no more than 5 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing, Ice fishing<br>Catch and Release: For species with defined harvest seasons, targeted catch and release angling can occur outside of harvest season, using artificial lures and flies except on those waters/areas that are closed to fishing.<br>Note: Daily Limits cannot be combined between rivers/streams and lakes/ponds.<br><i>Other species, and lakes and ponds: Table 1, p. 54.</i>",
