  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 4 entries, tap to read</summary><i>Covers about 15.2 km of the 146.0 km mapped.</i><br><b>Winooski River · Winooski/ Burlington · Chittenden</b> (p. 46)<br>Lake Champlain to the first railroad bridge (approximately 9 miles) in Winooski and Burlington. (R–LC)<br>• Lake Champlain Boundaries<br><i>Table</i> 2 · <i>ANS</i> EW<br><br><i>Covers about 1.4 km of the 146.0 km mapped.</i><br><b>Winooski River · Winooski/ Burlington · Chittenden</b> (p. 46)<br>From the Winooski One Hydro Dam west of Main Street (US 7) in Winooski and Burlington and extending downstream to the downstream side of the first railroad bridge. (R–LC)<br>• Closed to Fishing: March 16–May 31<br><i>Table</i> 2<br><br><i>Covers about 6.9 km of the 146.0 km mapped.</i><br><b>Winooski River · Bolton/ Duxbury/ Waterbury · Chittenden/ Washington</b> (p. 46)<br>From Preston Brook mouth upstream (approximately 4.4 miles) to the Ridley Brook mouth.<br>• Trout: length limit, 10” to 16” protected slot (all fish 10” to 16” must be released); daily limit, 2 trout, only 1 greater than 16”<br><i>Table</i> 1<br><br><i>Covers about 8.4 km of the 146.0 km mapped.</i><br><b>Winooski River · Duxbury/ Waterbury · Washington</b> (p. 46)<br>Winooski River in Duxbury and Waterbury, from the top of the Bolton Dam in Duxbury and Waterbury upstream to the Route 2 bridge (east side of Waterbury Village).<br>• Brook, Brown, and Rainbow Trout: season, second Saturday in April to Oct. 31; length limit, none; daily limit, total number of brook trout, brown trout, and rainbow trout, no more than 2<br><i>Table</i> 1<br><br><i>The index's own note</i> (p. 40): Waters listed in this index have special regulations that override the general regulations and must be followed.<br><br><i>Lake Champlain water: the index sends this river's lowest reach to Table 2.</i><br><b>Lake Champlain Waters</b> (p. 56)<br>Lake Champlain includes setbacks at the same level and major tributaries to the lake to the following boundaries:<br>• Winooski River to the Winooski One hydropower dam west of Main Street (U.S. Route 7) in Winooski and Burlington.<br><b>Table 2: General Fishing Regulations for Lake Champlain</b> (p. 58)<br>General Fishing Regulations for Lake Champlain include the setbacks at the same water level and the lower portion of its tributaries as defined on page 56. Spawning waters are not included.<br>Lake Champlain Open-Water Fishing—Number of Lines/Rods: A person may take fish only by using not more than two lines of which he or she has immediate control over all lines. Each line may not have more than two baited hooks or three artificial flies or two lures with or without bait.<br>• Brook Trout and Brown Trout and Rainbow Trout · <i>Open season for harvest:</i> All year · <i>Minimum length:</i> 12” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of brook + brown + rainbows = no more than 3 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water and Ice fishing<br>• Lake Trout · <i>Open season for harvest:</i> All year · <i>Minimum length:</i> 15” · <i>Daily limit:</i> 3 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water and Ice fishing<br>• Landlocked Atlantic Salmon · <i>Open season for harvest:</i> All year · <i>Minimum length:</i> 15” · <i>Daily limit:</i> 2 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water and Ice fishing<br>• Largemouth and Smallmouth Bass · <i>Open season for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in June to Nov. 30 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 12” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of largemouth + smallmouth = no more than 5 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>Catch and Release: For species with defined harvest seasons, targeted catch and release angling can occur outside of harvest season, using artificial lures and flies except on those waters/areas that are closed to fishing.<br><i>Other species: Table 2, p. 58.</i><br><br><i>Baitfish restricted water, the tag in the reach cell.</i><br>Baitfish Zones: see page 27 for statewide map. Restricted waters: (R-BK)=Batten Kill River; (R-LC)=Lake Champlain; (R-M)=Lake Memphremagog; (R-CT)=Connecticut River (p. 40)<br>Baitfish used or harvested in these waterbodies may NOT be transported to or used in a different waterbody (p. 27)<br><b>Restricted Waters</b> (p. 28)<br>• Lake Champlain (R–LC) (see 10 App. §122 Section 7.0) including setbacks at the same level and tributaries to the following boundaries:<br>– Winooski River to the Winooski One hydropower dam west of Main Street (US 7) in Winooski and Burlington<br><br>1 – Aquatic Nuisance Species (ANS): EW=Eurasian Watermilfoil; WC=Water Chestnut; WD=Whirling Disease (p. 40)</details><br><br><b>Standard rule: Table 1: General Fishing Regulations for Vermont.</b> (p. 54)<br>Waterbody-specific regulations listed in Index of Rivers and Streams or the Index of Lakes and Ponds override the General Regulations<br>Regulations for all waterbodies NOT listed in the Index of Rivers and Streams (page 40) or the Index of Lakes and Ponds (page 48) fall under this table.<br>Note different regulation for River/Stream and Lake/Pond.<br>• Anadromous Atlantic Salmon · All · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> No open season · <i>Minimum length:</i> NA · <i>Daily limit:</i> 0 · <i>Legal methods:</i> None<br>• Brook Trout and Brown Trout and Rainbow Trout · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> None · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of brook + brown + rainbow = no more than 8 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Lake Trout · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 18” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of lake trout + landlocked salmon = no more than 2 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Landlocked Atlantic Salmon · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 17” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of lake trout + landlocked salmon = no more than 2 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Largemouth and Smallmouth Bass · All · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in June to March 15 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 10” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of largemouth + smallmouth = no more than 5 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing, Ice fishing<br>Catch and Release: For species with defined harvest seasons, targeted catch and release angling can occur outside of harvest season, using artificial lures and flies except on those waters/areas that are closed to fishing.<br>Note: Daily Limits cannot be combined between rivers/streams and lakes/ponds.<br><i>Other species, and lakes and ponds: Table 1, p. 54.</i>",
