  parkRegs:"<details><summary>This river's own rules — 3 entries, tap to read</summary><i>Covers about 11.4 km of the 71.9 km mapped.</i><br><b>Black River (Memphremagog Tributary) · Coventry · Orleans</b> (p. 41)<br>From Lake Memphremagog upstream to 600’ below the falls at Old Harman Mill in Coventry.<br>• Rainbow Trout and Brown Trout: length limit, minimum length 10”; daily limit, 2 trout<br><i>Table</i> 1<br><br><i>Covers about 0.2 km of the 71.9 km mapped.</i><br><b>Black River (Memphremagog Tributary) · Coventry · Orleans</b> (p. 41)<br>From 600’ below the falls at Old Harman Mill in Coventry upstream to the top of the falls at Old Harman Mill in Coventry.<br>• Closed to Fishing: March 15 through May 31<br>• Rainbow Trout and Brown Trout: length limit, minimum length 10”; daily limit, 2 trout<br><i>Table</i> 1<br><br><i>Covers about 11.9 km of the 71.9 km mapped.</i><br><b>Black River (Memphremagog Tributary) · Newport City, Coventry · Orleans</b> (p. 41)<br>Old Harman Mill in Coventry upstream to the downstream side of the VT Routes 14/58 bridge in Irasburg.<br>• Rainbow Trout and Brown Trout: length limit, minimum length 10”; daily limit, 2 trout<br><i>Table</i> 1<br><br><i>The index's own note</i> (p. 40): Waters listed in this index have special regulations that override the general regulations and must be followed.<br><br><i>Baitfish restricted water, the tag in the reach cell.</i><br>Baitfish Zones: see page 27 for statewide map. Restricted waters: (R-BK)=Batten Kill River; (R-LC)=Lake Champlain; (R-M)=Lake Memphremagog; (R-CT)=Connecticut River (p. 40)<br>Baitfish used or harvested in these waterbodies may NOT be transported to or used in a different waterbody (p. 27)<br><b>Restricted Waters</b> (p. 28)<br>• Lake Memphremagog (R–M) including the following tributaries:<br>– Black River to the top of the falls at Old Harmon Mill in the town of Coventry</details><br><br><b>Standard rule: Table 1: General Fishing Regulations for Vermont.</b> (p. 54)<br>Waterbody-specific regulations listed in Index of Rivers and Streams or the Index of Lakes and Ponds override the General Regulations<br>Regulations for all waterbodies NOT listed in the Index of Rivers and Streams (page 40) or the Index of Lakes and Ponds (page 48) fall under this table.<br>Note different regulation for River/Stream and Lake/Pond.<br>• Anadromous Atlantic Salmon · All · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> No open season · <i>Minimum length:</i> NA · <i>Daily limit:</i> 0 · <i>Legal methods:</i> None<br>• Brook Trout and Brown Trout and Rainbow Trout · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> None · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of brook + brown + rainbow = no more than 8 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Lake Trout · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 18” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of lake trout + landlocked salmon = no more than 2 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Landlocked Atlantic Salmon · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 17” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of lake trout + landlocked salmon = no more than 2 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Largemouth and Smallmouth Bass · All · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in June to March 15 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 10” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of largemouth + smallmouth = no more than 5 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing, Ice fishing<br>Catch and Release: For species with defined harvest seasons, targeted catch and release angling can occur outside of harvest season, using artificial lures and flies except on those waters/areas that are closed to fishing.<br>Note: Daily Limits cannot be combined between rivers/streams and lakes/ponds.<br><i>Other species, and lakes and ponds: Table 1, p. 54.</i>",
