  parkRegs:"<i>Covers about 6.5 km of the 15.2 km mapped.</i><br><b>Walloomsac River · Bennington and Shaftsbury · Bennington</b> (p. 45)<br>From the VT/NY border in Bennington upstream to the top of the former Vermont Tissues Plant Dam (downstream of Murphy Road) in Bennington.<br>• Brook, Brown, and Rainbow Trout: season, second Sat in April to Oct. 31; length limit, none; daily limit, total number of brook trout, brown trout, and rainbow trout, no more than 2<br><i>Table</i> 1<br><br><i>The index's own note</i> (p. 40): Waters listed in this index have special regulations that override the general regulations and must be followed.<br><br><b>Standard rule: Table 1: General Fishing Regulations for Vermont.</b> (p. 54)<br>Waterbody-specific regulations listed in Index of Rivers and Streams or the Index of Lakes and Ponds override the General Regulations<br>Regulations for all waterbodies NOT listed in the Index of Rivers and Streams (page 40) or the Index of Lakes and Ponds (page 48) fall under this table.<br>Note different regulation for River/Stream and Lake/Pond.<br>• Anadromous Atlantic Salmon · All · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> No open season · <i>Minimum length:</i> NA · <i>Daily limit:</i> 0 · <i>Legal methods:</i> None<br>• Brook Trout and Brown Trout and Rainbow Trout · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> None · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of brook + brown + rainbow = no more than 8 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Lake Trout · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 18” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of lake trout + landlocked salmon = no more than 2 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Landlocked Atlantic Salmon · River/Stream · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in April to Oct. 31 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 17” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of lake trout + landlocked salmon = no more than 2 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing<br>• Largemouth and Smallmouth Bass · All · <i>Open seasons for harvest:</i> 2nd Sat. in June to March 15 · <i>Minimum length:</i> 10” · <i>Daily limit:</i> Total of largemouth + smallmouth = no more than 5 · <i>Legal methods:</i> Open-water fishing, Ice fishing<br>Catch and Release: For species with defined harvest seasons, targeted catch and release angling can occur outside of harvest season, using artificial lures and flies except on those waters/areas that are closed to fishing.<br>Note: Daily Limits cannot be combined between rivers/streams and lakes/ponds.<br><i>Other species, and lakes and ponds: Table 1, p. 54.</i>",
