  bounds:[[43.74887,-110.74454],[43.77818,-110.71694]],
  blurb:"The postcard: a glacial lake sitting directly under Teewinot and the Grand, with the shuttle boat crossing to Cascade Canyon. Busy at the trailhead end and quiet along the west shore.",
  fish:"Lake trout and cutthroat in very clear, very cold water. Clarity is the problem and the attraction — fish see everything.",
  regs:"Park lakes are <b>open to fishing year-round</b>. Lake creel is <b>six trout</b>, no more than three of them cutthroat, and no more than one cutthroat over sixteen inches. A <b>Wyoming fishing licence</b> is required — Grand Teton is fished under Wyoming regulations, not a park permit of its own. The park names Jenny among the lakes to paddle.",
