  blurb:"Hebgen Lake is the reservoir on the Madison just outside West Yellowstone, above Quake Lake.",
  fish:"Fished under Montana's Central District standard limits for lakes and reservoirs.",
  regs:"<i>Hebgen Lake has no entry of its own in the 2026 Central District Exceptions — the Central District standard limits apply.</i><br><br><b>Central District standard limits</b> — Combined trout (brown, rainbow, golden and cutthroat trout and arctic grayling), lakes/reservoirs: 5 daily and 10 in possession, includes cutthroat trout. Brook trout: 20 daily and in possession. Whitefish: 20 daily and 40 in possession.",
