  id:"holterlake", name:"Holter Lake", short:"Holter Lake", park:"montana", state:"MT", src:"nhd",
  areaKm2:14.7, at:[46.93983,-111.96175],
  bounds:[[46.87643,-112.01393],[46.99398,-111.91239]],
  blurb:"Holter Lake is the Missouri River reservoir through the Gates of the Mountains, north of Helena, held by Holter Dam near Wolf Creek. The outline is USGS NHD's, which draws a reservoir at its normal pool.",
  fish:"Brown trout are catch-and-release (anglers 14 and under may keep one), walleye are five a day with only one over 25 inches, and rainbow trout and kokanee five a day in any combination.",
  regs:"<b>HOLTER RESERVOIR</b><br><b>Up to American Bar Gulch (approximately 4.6 miles downstream from Hauser Dam)</b><br>• Catch-and-release for brown trout, except anglers 14 years of age or younger may take 1 brown trout daily and in possession, any size.<br>• Walleye: 5 daily, only 1 over 25 inches. Possession limit is twice the daily limit.<br>• Combined trout and kokanee salmon: 5 rainbow trout and kokanee salmon daily in any combination and 10 rainbow trout and kokanee salmon in possession in any combination.<br>• Yellow perch: 25 daily and 50 in possession.<br>• Northern pike: no limit.<br>• Hook and Line/Setlines: 6 lines with 2 hooks per line through the ice only.<br>• Spearing: open for northern pike through the ice.<br><i>— Montana FWP 2026 Fishing Regulations, Central District Exceptions to Standard Regulations, pp. 58–59</i><br><br><b>2026 General Fishing Season</b> — Lakes and Reservoirs: Open all year. Fishing is allowed at all hours during open fishing seasons unless otherwise specified in District Exceptions to Standard Regulations.<br><i>— Montana FWP 2026 Fishing Regulations, 2026 General Fishing Season, p. 4</i><br><br><b>Hook and Line Limits</b><br><b>Open Water</b> — Lakes and Reservoirs: 2 lines with 2 hooks per line. All lines must be attended and in the angler’s immediate control.<br><b>Ice Fishing</b> — Lakes and Reservoirs: 2 lines with 2 hooks per line through the ice on lakes, reservoirs, or ponds open to fishing. When a line is used through the ice, the angler need not be in immediate control, but must be in the vicinity and in visual contact with the line.<br><i>— Montana FWP 2026 Fishing Regulations, Central District standard regulations, p. 46</i><br><br><b>Central District Standard Daily and Possession Limits</b><br>Each angler may take all of the limits listed in the chart, unless otherwise noted in the Central District Exceptions. For species not listed, there are no limits on the number of fish that may be taken or possessed.<br>• <b>Brook Trout</b>: 20 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Combined Trout</b> (includes brown trout, rainbow trout, golden trout, cutthroat trout, and arctic grayling): Lakes/Reservoirs: 5 daily and 10 in possession, includes cutthroat trout.<br>• <b>Lake Trout</b>: 3 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Bass</b>: 5 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Burbot (Ling)</b>: 5 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Channel Catfish</b>: 10 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Crappie</b>: 15 daily and 30 in possession.<br>• <b>Northern Pike</b>: 10 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Pallid Sturgeon</b>: None - this is an endangered species and all fish must be released immediately. All waters are closed to fishing for pallid sturgeon.<br>• <b>Salmon (Kokanee &amp; Chinook)</b>: 10 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Sauger/Walleye</b>: 5 daily, only 2 may be sauger. Possession limit is 10, only 4 may be sauger.<br>• <b>Shovelnose Sturgeon</b>: 5 daily and in possession, none over 40 inches.<br>• <b>Tiger Muskie</b>: 1 daily and in possession, must be over 40 inches.<br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: 20 daily and 40 in possession.<br><i>— Montana FWP 2026 Fishing Regulations, Central District Standard Daily and Possession Limits, p. 49</i>",
  regsNote:"From Montana Fish, Wildlife &amp; Parks' <b>2026 Fishing Regulations</b> — the lake's own entry in the Central District Exceptions to Standard Regulations, then the Central District standard. An entry takes the place of the standard for the items it lists; the standard covers everything else.",
