  blurb:"Cooney Reservoir is on Red Lodge Creek between Columbus and Red Lodge. The outline is USGS NHD's, which draws a reservoir at its normal pool.",
  fish:"No entry of its own — the Central District standard below applies.",
  regs:"<i>Cooney Reservoir has no entry of its own in the 2026 Central District Exceptions to Standard Regulations — the Central District standard regulations apply.</i><br><br><b>2026 General Fishing Season</b> — Lakes and Reservoirs: Open all year. Fishing is allowed at all hours during open fishing seasons unless otherwise specified in District Exceptions to Standard Regulations.<br><i>— Montana FWP 2026 Fishing Regulations, 2026 General Fishing Season, p. 4</i><br><br><b>Hook and Line Limits</b><br><b>Open Water</b> — Lakes and Reservoirs: 2 lines with 2 hooks per line. All lines must be attended and in the angler’s immediate control.<br><b>Ice Fishing</b> — Lakes and Reservoirs: 2 lines with 2 hooks per line through the ice on lakes, reservoirs, or ponds open to fishing. When a line is used through the ice, the angler need not be in immediate control, but must be in the vicinity and in visual contact with the line.<br><i>— Montana FWP 2026 Fishing Regulations, Central District standard regulations, p. 46</i><br><br><b>Central District Standard Daily and Possession Limits</b><br>Each angler may take all of the limits listed in the chart, unless otherwise noted in the Central District Exceptions. For species not listed, there are no limits on the number of fish that may be taken or possessed.<br>• <b>Brook Trout</b>: 20 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Combined Trout</b> (includes brown trout, rainbow trout, golden trout, cutthroat trout, and arctic grayling): Lakes/Reservoirs: 5 daily and 10 in possession, includes cutthroat trout.<br>• <b>Lake Trout</b>: 3 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Bass</b>: 5 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Burbot (Ling)</b>: 5 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Channel Catfish</b>: 10 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Crappie</b>: 15 daily and 30 in possession.<br>• <b>Northern Pike</b>: 10 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Pallid Sturgeon</b>: None - this is an endangered species and all fish must be released immediately. All waters are closed to fishing for pallid sturgeon.<br>• <b>Salmon (Kokanee &amp; Chinook)</b>: 10 daily and in possession.<br>• <b>Sauger/Walleye</b>: 5 daily, only 2 may be sauger. Possession limit is 10, only 4 may be sauger.<br>• <b>Shovelnose Sturgeon</b>: 5 daily and in possession, none over 40 inches.<br>• <b>Tiger Muskie</b>: 1 daily and in possession, must be over 40 inches.<br>• <b>Whitefish</b>: 20 daily and 40 in possession.<br><i>— Montana FWP 2026 Fishing Regulations, Central District Standard Daily and Possession Limits, p. 49</i>",
  regsNote:"From Montana Fish, Wildlife &amp; Parks' <b>2026 Fishing Regulations</b>. The lake has no entry of its own in the Central District Exceptions, so the Central District standard season, hook and line limits and daily limits apply, quoted here.",
