  regs:"<b>Black Hills exceptions to statewide harvest and length limits</b><br>1 - BLACK HILLS FISH MANAGEMENT AREA<br>TROUT: Only one trout 14” or longer caught from any Black Hills stream may be included in the daily limit (does not apply to reservoirs). No high grading of trout is permitted in the management area.<br>LAKE TROUT/SPLAKE: Daily limit 1; Minimum length 24”<br>Waters not listed as Black Hills exceptions fall under statewide harvest and length limits on page 18.<br><i>— SD GFP, 2026 South Dakota Fishing Handbook, Black Hills Exceptions to Statewide Harvest and Length Limits, p. 31</i><br><br><b>Statewide harvest and length limits</b> <i>(daily limit / possession limit)</i><br>• Walleye (includes walleye/sauger/saugeye) — 4 (only one 20” or longer) / 8<br>• Northern pike — 6 / 12<br>• Muskellunge, tiger muskie — Catch and release only<br>• Trout, salmon, splake (any combination) — 5 / 10<br>• Largemouth/smallmouth bass (any combination) — 5 / 10<br>• Yellow perch — 15 / 30<br>• Crappie — 15 / 30<br>• Sunfish (bluegill, green, pumpkinseed, redear, Orangespotted in any combination) — 15 / 30<br>• Catfish (any combination) — 10 (only one flathead catfish 30” or longer) / 20<br>• Sturgeon — With the exception of a catch and release season for lake sturgeon on Big Stone Lake from June 16 to April 14, the season is closed for all sturgeon species.<br>• Paddlefish — Available by special permit only<br>• Smelt — 5 gallons / No possession<br>• White bass/rock bass — No limit<br>• Lake herring/lake whitefish/bullhead/rough fish — No limit<br><i>— SD GFP, 2026 South Dakota Fishing Handbook, Statewide Harvest and Length Limits, p. 18</i><br><br><b>Waters closed to taking of bait using seines, nets, and traps</b><br>… and these individual waters:<br>Pennington County – Deerfield, Pactola, and Sheridan<br><i>— SD GFP, 2026 South Dakota Fishing Handbook, Non-Commercial Bait Regulations, p. 39</i><br><br><b>Aquatic invasive species infested waters</b><br>• SHERIDAN LAKE — Rudd, Curly Pondweed<br>For a complete list of AIS regulations and the most current list of AIS infested waters, visit SDLEASTWANTED.SD.GOV.<br><i>— SD GFP, 2026 South Dakota Fishing Handbook, Aquatic Invasive Species Infested Waters, p. 61</i>",
  regsNote:"From South Dakota Game, Fish and Parks' <b>2026 South Dakota Fishing Handbook</b>: the Black Hills Fish Management Area rule, then the statewide limits and the bait rule that names the lake, word for word with pages. The handbook's general rules (bait, lines and hooks, spearing and archery, set-lines, boating) aren't reproduced, except lines in them that name this lake. Read the current handbook before you fish.",
